# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# IFC elements made native: walls, floors, roofs and straight grid axes read from an IFC file
# become the model's own walls and plates (with storeys, wall types from
# their material layers, and their openings with door and window types),
# so that everything works on them as on drawn ones: grips, joins, Tab's
# boundary sketch, properties, IFC export. What cannot be made native (a
# curved wall, a wall that is not one straight extrusion, a sloped slab)
# stays an imported read-only element (`bim_ifc_read.dl`).
#
# A wall: the straight line of its Axis representation (or else its
# footprint's longest side) gives its direction; its body's vertical
# extrusion gives its footprint, foot and head; the footprint's width
# across the line its thickness, and the line moved to the footprint's
# middle its centre line, ended where the axis ends. Its layers come from
# its IfcMaterialLayerSetUsage (else one layer of its material, as thick as
# the footprint). Its openings (IfcRelVoidsElement) become openings where
# their bodies cross it, a door when an IfcDoor fills them.
# A slab (IfcSlab, also a roof's): the outline of its vertical extrusion at
# its top, its depth its thickness.
# A column, beam or pile (IfcColumn, IfcBeam, IfcPile): one straight
# extrusion of a rectangle, circle or I-shape becomes a linear element from
# its profile's centre along its sweep, of a linear type of that size and
# material (an I-shape as its outer rectangle).
#
# A wall or member in any other representation (a B-rep, a mapped shape, a
# boolean) is measured from its triangles: a wall when they are an upright
# prism on a straight footprint, a member when every corner lies on its
# section's rectangle or circle. A member of another section (an I, a hollow
# section) is kept apart as `shaped`, with its section's area, for the
# profile catalogue to give it its type (`elements/linear/
# bim_ifc_profiles.dl`); without one it stays an imported element.
#
# A measured wall may have holes: upright, right through it, each a
# rectangle, and each filled by a door or window (measured from its
# triangles too). They become its openings; a wall with a hole nothing
# fills stays imported, for the model has no opening without a filling.
#
# A wall given as a mesh with its openings already cut (as IFC4 exports
# write a wall that hosts doors or windows) takes its openings from its
# IfcOpeningElements, as an extruded wall does: it is its box less those
# openings when its volume says so, its ends maybe cut for a join.
#
# Pipe, duct and cable carrier segments (IfcPipeSegment, IfcDuctSegment,
# IfcCableCarrierSegment) and members (IfcMember: mullions, studs) become
# linear elements too, of the pipe, duct, cable tray and frame roles. A
# segment is hollow: it counts by its outline, round when no corner lies
# outside the circle in its box, else the rectangle of its box.
#
# A door or window that stands between two pieces of wall on one line (the
# file gives the wall in pieces round its frame: one either side, maybe one
# under it and one over it) has no wall to be an opening of. The pieces are
# then made one wall, from the far end of the one to the far end of the
# other, with the gap between them as its opening; the model lists the
# pieces' GlobalIds as taken over into that wall.
import ifc/bim_ifc_read.dl
import ifc/bim_ifc_psets.dl
import ifc/bim_ifc_grid.dl
import bim/bim_grid_height.dl

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc native opening record
    members:
        along as a 64 bit floating-point number
        width as a 64 bit floating-point number
        height as a 64 bit floating-point number
        sillHeight as a 64 bit floating-point number
        isDoor as a boolean

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc native wall record
    members:
        storey as an integer
        start as a cad vector2
        finish as a cad vector2
        foot as a 64 bit floating-point number
        head as a 64 bit floating-point number
        layers as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim layer record)
        openings as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc native opening record)

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc native slab record
    members:
        storey as an integer
        outline as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector2)
        top as a 64 bit floating-point number
        thickness as a 64 bit floating-point number
        material as a string

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc native linear record
    members:
        storey as an integer
        start as a cad vector3
        finish as a cad vector3
        width as a 64 bit floating-point number
        depth as a 64 bit floating-point number
        round as a boolean
        material as a string
        role as an integer
        turn as a 64 bit floating-point number
        # A shaped member's (its `round` then says its section's outline is
        # a circle): the area of its section, whether it has corners near a
        # middle line of its section (a web), whether its web lies along
        # its width, and the catalogue profile it was fitted to (0 none).
        sectionArea as a 64 bit floating-point number
        webbed as a boolean
        webAcross as a boolean
        catalogueKey as a 64 bit integer

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc native set record
    members:
        storeyNames as the type of (a cad topology list of a string)
        storeyElevations as the type of (a cad topology list of a 64 bit floating-point number)
        walls as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc native wall record)
        slabs as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc native slab record)
        linears as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc native linear record)
        grids as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc native grid record)
        # The instances made native (walls, slabs, the doors and windows in
        # their openings), for the import to leave out.
        skipped as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        # The STEP instance each storey, wall, slab and linear element came
        # from, and the property sets of those instances (keyed by them).
        storeySources as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        wallSources as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        slabSources as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        linearSources as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        psets as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim pset entry record)
        # The members of a section the model has no plain type for, and the
        # STEP instance of each.
        shaped as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc native linear record)
        shapedSources as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)
        # For each wall the wall it was made part of (a piece beside a door
        # or window joined to the piece on its other side), or -1.
        wallAbsorbed as the type of (a cad topology list of an integer)

# The extrusions of a representation in the world: the corners of each
# one's profile at its start (`bottoms`) and its sweep (`sweeps`); `found`
# false when an item is not an extrusion (a boolean's first operand
# counts).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc extrusion set record
    members:
        found as a boolean
        bottoms as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector3)
        sweeps as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector3)
        # Where each extrusion's corners start in `bottoms`, and the first
        # one's outer ring alone (for a slab's outline).
        firstRing as the type of (a cad topology list of a cad vector3)

function the bim ifc extrusions of representation {integer:representationId} through {bim ifc frame record:frame} in {a pointer to a bim ifc reader record:reader}:
    execute:
        set result to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc extrusion set record, false, a cad topology list of a cad vector3, a cad topology list of a cad vector3, a cad topology list of a cad vector3)
        if (bim step file (reader's stepFile) holds representationId) = false:
            return result
        set representationValue to the bim step instance representationId in (reader's stepFile)
        set items to the bim step argument 3 of representationValue
        set accepted to (the bim step count of items in representationValue) > 0
        loop cursor from 0 to the bim step count of items in representationValue:
            set itemId to the bim step reference of (the bim step member cursor of items in representationValue) in representationValue
            # Through booleans to their first operand.
            set descending to true
            set depthGuard to 0
            loop while descending and (depthGuard < 6):
                set depthGuard to depthGuard + 1
                set descending to false
                if (bim step instance itemId is a "IFCBOOLEANCLIPPINGRESULT" in (reader's stepFile)) or (bim step instance itemId is a "IFCBOOLEANRESULT" in (reader's stepFile)):
                    set booleanValue to the bim step instance itemId in (reader's stepFile)
                    set itemId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 1 of booleanValue) in booleanValue
                    free bim step instance booleanValue
                    set descending to true
            if accepted and (bim step instance itemId is a "IFCEXTRUDEDAREASOLID" in (reader's stepFile)):
                set itemValue to the bim step instance itemId in (reader's stepFile)
                set solidFrame to the bim ifc axes (the bim ifc placement axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 1 of itemValue) in itemValue) in reader) within frame
                set direction to the bim ifc ratios (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 2 of itemValue) in itemValue) or (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0) in reader
                set depth to (the bim step number of (the bim step argument 3 of itemValue) in itemValue) * reader's lengthScale
                set rings to an empty list of the type of (an empty list of a cad vector2)
                set outerFlags to an empty list of a boolean
                append bim ifc profile (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 0 of itemValue) in itemValue) outlines into rings marking outerFlags through (the bim ifc identity axes) in reader
                free bim step instance itemValue
                if (the length of rings) = 0:
                    set accepted to false
                else:
                    set sweep to (the bim ifc turned (the bim ifc unit of direction or (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0)) through solidFrame) scaled by depth
                    append sweep to (result's sweeps's values)
                    set ring to the item at 0 in rings
                    loop corner from 0 to the length of ring:
                        set flat to the item at corner in ring
                        set placed to the bim ifc placed (a cad vector3 with x flat's x, y flat's y and z 0.0) through solidFrame
                        append placed to (result's bottoms's values)
                        if (the length of (result's sweeps's values)) = 1:
                            append placed to (result's firstRing's values)
                loop ringCursor from 0 to the length of rings:
                    free (the item at ringCursor in rings)
                free rings
                free outerFlags
            else:
                set accepted to false
        free bim step instance representationValue
        set result's found to accepted and ((the length of (result's sweeps's values)) > 0)
        return result

# The 2D points of the Axis representation of shape `shapeId` through
# `frame` (two for a straight axis; none when it has none).
function the bim ifc axis of shape {integer:shapeId} through {bim ifc frame record:frame} in {a pointer to a bim ifc reader record:reader}:
    execute:
        set found to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
        if (bim step instance shapeId is a "IFCPRODUCTDEFINITIONSHAPE" in (reader's stepFile)) = false:
            return found
        set shapeValue to the bim step instance shapeId in (reader's stepFile)
        set representations to the bim step argument 2 of shapeValue
        loop cursor from 0 to the bim step count of representations in shapeValue:
            set representationId to the bim step reference of (the bim step member cursor of representations in shapeValue) in shapeValue
            set representationValue to the bim step instance representationId in (reader's stepFile)
            if ((the bim step string of (the bim step argument 1 of representationValue) in representationValue) = (the string form of "Axis")) and ((the length of (found's values)) = 0):
                set items to the bim step argument 3 of representationValue
                if (the bim step count of items in representationValue) > 0:
                    set curveId to the bim step reference of (the bim step member 0 of items in representationValue) in representationValue
                    if bim step instance curveId is a "IFCPOLYLINE" in (reader's stepFile):
                        set points to the bim ifc polyline of curveId in reader
                        if (the length of points) = 2:
                            loop pointCursor from 0 to 2:
                                set local to the item at pointCursor in points
                                set placed to the bim ifc placed local through frame
                                append (a cad vector2 with x placed's x and y placed's y) to (found's values)
                        free points
            free bim step instance representationValue
        free bim step instance shapeValue
        return found

# A material named in IFC as one of the slice's (by English and Dutch
# words), else its own name.
function the bim native material of {a string:materialName}:
    execute:
        set lowered to the lowercase form of materialName
        if ((lowered contains "brick") or (lowered contains "baksteen")) or ((lowered contains "metsel") or (lowered contains "masonry")):
            return the string form of "brick"
        if (lowered contains "kalkzand") or (lowered contains "sand-lime"):
            return the string form of "sand-lime"
        if (lowered contains "beton") or (lowered contains "concrete"):
            return the string form of "concrete"
        if ((lowered contains "isola") or (lowered contains "insul")) or ((lowered contains "wool") or (lowered contains "pir")):
            return the string form of "insulation"
        if (lowered contains "gips") or ((lowered contains "gypsum") or (lowered contains "plaster")):
            return the string form of "gypsum"
        if (lowered contains "hout") or ((lowered contains "timber") or (lowered contains "wood")):
            return the string form of "timber"
        if (lowered contains "staal") or (lowered contains "steel"):
            return the string form of "steel"
        if ((lowered contains "lucht") or (lowered contains "spouw")) or ((lowered contains "air") or (lowered contains "cavity")):
            return the string form of "air"
        if (the length of materialName) = 0:
            return the string form of "concrete"
        return materialName

# The name of IfcMaterial `materialId` (empty when it is none).
function the bim ifc material name of {integer:materialId} in {a pointer to a bim ifc reader record:reader}:
    execute:
        if (bim step instance materialId is a "IFCMATERIAL" in (reader's stepFile)) = false:
            return the string form of ""
        set materialValue to the bim step instance materialId in (reader's stepFile)
        set named to the bim step string of (the bim step argument 0 of materialValue) in materialValue
        free bim step instance materialValue
        return named

# The layers of material association `associatedId` (an IfcMaterialLayer-
# SetUsage, an IfcMaterialLayerSet, an IfcMaterialList or an IfcMaterial):
# for a single material, one layer `fallbackThickness` thick.
function the bim ifc layers of material {integer:associatedId} thick {a 64 bit floating-point number:fallbackThickness} in {a pointer to a bim ifc reader record:reader}:
    execute:
        set layerList to a cad topology list of a bim layer record
        set setId to associatedId
        if bim step instance associatedId is a "IFCMATERIALLAYERSETUSAGE" in (reader's stepFile):
            set usageValue to the bim step instance associatedId in (reader's stepFile)
            set setId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 0 of usageValue) in usageValue
            free bim step instance usageValue
        if bim step instance setId is a "IFCMATERIALLAYERSET" in (reader's stepFile):
            set setValue to the bim step instance setId in (reader's stepFile)
            set layerNodes to the bim step argument 0 of setValue
            loop cursor from 0 to the bim step count of layerNodes in setValue:
                set layerId to the bim step reference of (the bim step member cursor of layerNodes in setValue) in setValue
                set layerValue to the bim step instance layerId in (reader's stepFile)
                set layerMaterial to the bim ifc material name of (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 0 of layerValue) in layerValue) in reader
                set layerThickness to (the bim step number of (the bim step argument 1 of layerValue) in layerValue) * reader's lengthScale
                free bim step instance layerValue
                if layerThickness > 0.0005:
                    append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the bim native material of layerMaterial, layerThickness)) to (layerList's values)
            free bim step instance setValue
            return layerList
        set single to the bim ifc material name of associatedId in reader
        if bim step instance associatedId is a "IFCMATERIALLIST" in (reader's stepFile):
            set listValue to the bim step instance associatedId in (reader's stepFile)
            set listed to the bim step argument 0 of listValue
            if (the bim step count of listed in listValue) > 0:
                set single to the bim ifc material name of (the bim step reference of (the bim step member 0 of listed in listValue) in listValue) in reader
            free bim step instance listValue
        append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the bim native material of single, fallbackThickness)) to (layerList's values)
        return layerList

# The section of a straight member: its profile's size (a rectangle, a
# circle's diameter, an I-shape's outer rectangle), the centre where its
# extrusion starts and its sweep in the world, and its profile's x axis;
# `found` false for anything else (several items, other profiles).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc section record
    members:
        found as a boolean
        width as a 64 bit floating-point number
        depth as a 64 bit floating-point number
        round as a boolean
        centre as a cad vector3
        sweep as a cad vector3
        xAxis as a cad vector3

function the bim ifc section of representation {integer:representationId} through {bim ifc frame record:frame} in {a pointer to a bim ifc reader record:reader}:
    execute:
        set origin to a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
        set result to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc section record, false, 0.0, 0.0, false, origin, origin, origin)
        if (bim step file (reader's stepFile) holds representationId) = false:
            return result
        set representationValue to the bim step instance representationId in (reader's stepFile)
        set items to the bim step argument 3 of representationValue
        set itemId to -1
        if (the bim step count of items in representationValue) = 1:
            set itemId to the bim step reference of (the bim step member 0 of items in representationValue) in representationValue
        free bim step instance representationValue
        if (itemId < 0) or ((bim step instance itemId is a "IFCEXTRUDEDAREASOLID" in (reader's stepFile)) = false):
            return result
        set itemValue to the bim step instance itemId in (reader's stepFile)
        set solidFrame to the bim ifc axes (the bim ifc placement axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 1 of itemValue) in itemValue) in reader) within frame
        set direction to the bim ifc ratios (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 2 of itemValue) in itemValue) or (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0) in reader
        set depthValue to (the bim step number of (the bim step argument 3 of itemValue) in itemValue) * reader's lengthScale
        set profileId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 0 of itemValue) in itemValue
        free bim step instance itemValue
        set profileValue to the bim step instance profileId in (reader's stepFile)
        set profileType to profileValue's typeName
        set profileFrame to the bim ifc axes (the bim ifc placement axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 2 of profileValue) in profileValue) in reader) within solidFrame
        set first to (the bim step number of (the bim step argument 3 of profileValue) in profileValue) * reader's lengthScale
        set second to (the bim step number of (the bim step argument 4 of profileValue) in profileValue) * reader's lengthScale
        free bim step instance profileValue
        set known to true
        if (profileType = (the string form of "IFCRECTANGLEPROFILEDEF")) or ((profileType = (the string form of "IFCISHAPEPROFILEDEF")) or (profileType = (the string form of "IFCRECTANGLEHOLLOWPROFILEDEF"))):
            set result's width to first
            set result's depth to second
        else if (profileType = (the string form of "IFCCIRCLEPROFILEDEF")) or (profileType = (the string form of "IFCCIRCLEHOLLOWPROFILEDEF")):
            set result's width to 2.0 * first
            set result's depth to 2.0 * first
            set result's round to true
        else:
            set known to false
        if known and ((result's width > 0.001) and (depthValue > 0.01)):
            set result's found to true
            set result's centre to profileFrame's origin
            set result's sweep to (the bim ifc turned (the bim ifc unit of direction or (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0)) through solidFrame) scaled by depthValue
            set result's xAxis to profileFrame's xAxis
        return result

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- solids measured from their triangles

# The triangles of representation `representationId` through `frame`, three
# points each (none when it has no geometry).
function the bim ifc corners of representation {integer:representationId} through {bim ifc frame record:frame} in {a pointer to a bim ifc reader record:reader}:
    execute:
        set cornerList to an empty list of a cad vector3
        if (bim step file (reader's stepFile) holds representationId) = false:
            return cornerList
        set painted to an empty bim ifc painted mesh
        set noColour to -1
        add bim ifc representation representationId through frame coloured noColour to (the address of painted) in reader
        loop groupCursor from 0 to the length of (painted's groups):
            set colourGroup to the item at groupCursor in (painted's groups)
            set indexList to colourGroup's triangles's values
            loop indexCursor from 0 to the length of indexList:
                append (the item at (the item at indexCursor in indexList) in (colourGroup's positions's values)) to cornerList
        free bim ifc painted (the address of painted)
        return cornerList

# The direction most of the edges of the triangles `cornerList` run in, by
# their length (seen in plan when `onPlan`); of length 0 when there is none.
function the bim ifc main run of {a pointer to a list:cornerList} seen in plan {boolean:onPlan}:
    execute:
        set runList to an empty list of a cad vector3
        set weightList to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        set longestList to an empty list of a 64 bit floating-point number
        set cornerCount to the length of cornerList
        set firstCorner to 0
        loop while (firstCorner + 2) < cornerCount:
            loop sideIndex from 0 to 3:
                set fromPoint to the item at (firstCorner + sideIndex) in cornerList
                set toPoint to the item at (firstCorner + (the remainder of (sideIndex + 1) divided by 3)) in cornerList
                set edgeVector to the cad difference of toPoint and fromPoint
                if onPlan:
                    set edgeVector to a cad vector3 with x edgeVector's x, y edgeVector's y and z 0.0
                set edgeLength to the cad length of edgeVector
                if edgeLength >= 0.02:
                    set unitEdge to edgeVector scaled by (1.0 / edgeLength)
                    set matched to -1
                    loop runCursor from 0 to the length of runList:
                        if matched < 0:
                            if (the absolute value of (the cad dot of (the item at runCursor in runList) and unitEdge)) > 0.9999:
                                set matched to runCursor
                    if matched >= 0:
                        replace item at index matched in weightList with ((the item at matched in weightList) + edgeLength)
                        if edgeLength > (the item at matched in longestList):
                            replace item at index matched in longestList with edgeLength
                            replace item at index matched in runList with unitEdge
                    else if (the length of runList) < 64:
                        append unitEdge to runList
                        append edgeLength to weightList
                        append edgeLength to longestList
            set firstCorner to firstCorner + 3
        set mainRun to a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
        set mainWeight to 0.0
        loop runCursor from 0 to the length of runList:
            if (the item at runCursor in weightList) > mainWeight:
                set mainWeight to the item at runCursor in weightList
                set mainRun to the item at runCursor in runList
        free runList
        free weightList
        free longestList
        return mainRun

# From where to where the points `cornerList` reach along `axis`.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc span record
    members:
        low as a 64 bit floating-point number
        high as a 64 bit floating-point number

function the bim ifc span of {a pointer to a list:cornerList} along {cad vector3:axis}:
    execute:
        set reach to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc span record, 1.0e30, -1.0e30)
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of cornerList:
            set alongValue to the cad dot of (the item at cursor in cornerList) and axis
            set reach's low to the minimum of reach's low and alongValue
            set reach's high to the maximum of reach's high and alongValue
        return reach

# The volume the triangles `cornerList` enclose (a closed shell's).
function the bim ifc volume of {a pointer to a list:cornerList}:
    execute:
        set cornerCount to the length of cornerList
        if cornerCount < 3:
            return 0.0
        set anchor to the item at 0 in cornerList
        set sixfold to 0.0
        set firstCorner to 0
        loop while (firstCorner + 2) < cornerCount:
            set first to the cad difference of (the item at firstCorner in cornerList) and anchor
            set second to the cad difference of (the item at (firstCorner + 1) in cornerList) and anchor
            set third to the cad difference of (the item at (firstCorner + 2) in cornerList) and anchor
            set sixfold to sixfold + (the cad dot of first and (the cad cross of second and third))
            set firstCorner to firstCorner + 3
        return (the absolute value of sixfold) / 6.0

# The plan area of the triangles of `cornerList` that lie level at `height`.
function the bim ifc level area of {a pointer to a list:cornerList} at {a 64 bit floating-point number:height}:
    execute:
        set cornerCount to the length of cornerList
        set levelArea to 0.0
        set firstCorner to 0
        loop while (firstCorner + 2) < cornerCount:
            set first to the item at firstCorner in cornerList
            set second to the item at (firstCorner + 1) in cornerList
            set third to the item at (firstCorner + 2) in cornerList
            if ((the absolute value of (first's z - height)) < 0.002) and (((the absolute value of (second's z - height)) < 0.002) and ((the absolute value of (third's z - height)) < 0.002)):
                set levelArea to levelArea + ((the absolute value of (((second's x - first's x) * (third's y - first's y)) - ((third's x - first's x) * (second's y - first's y)))) * 0.5)
            set firstCorner to firstCorner + 3
        return levelArea

# A hole right through a measured wall, and a band of level triangles (see
# `the bim ifc level bands of`).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc wall hole record
    members:
        low as a 64 bit floating-point number
        high as a 64 bit floating-point number
        sill as a 64 bit floating-point number
        head as a 64 bit floating-point number

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc band record
    members:
        height as a 64 bit floating-point number
        low as a 64 bit floating-point number
        high as a 64 bit floating-point number
        area as a 64 bit floating-point number

# A wall measured from its triangles: `found` when they are an upright prism
# (its top as large as its foot, its volume their area times its height) on
# a footprint about a rectangle as thick as a wall; its centre line from
# `start` to `finish`, its foot and head, and its thickness.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc measured wall record
    members:
        found as a boolean
        start as a cad vector2
        finish as a cad vector2
        foot as a 64 bit floating-point number
        head as a 64 bit floating-point number
        thickness as a 64 bit floating-point number
        # Its holes, each from `low` to `high` along it from its start and
        # from `sill` to `head` in height.
        holes as the type of (a cad topology list of a bim ifc wall hole record)
        # Whether its box is a wall's at all (its line, foot, head and
        # thickness are then given, also when it is not `found`), and the
        # volume its triangles enclose.
        boxed as a boolean
        volume as a 64 bit floating-point number

# The level triangles of `cornerList` that face down (or up), gathered into
# bands: those at one height whose reaches along `axis` touch, with their
# area together. Only those higher than `lowLimit` and lower than
# `highLimit` count; reaches are measured from `origin` along the axis.
function the bim ifc level bands of {a pointer to a list:cornerList} along {cad vector3:axis} from {a 64 bit floating-point number:origin} facing down {boolean:facesDown} above {a 64 bit floating-point number:lowLimit} below {a 64 bit floating-point number:highLimit}:
    execute:
        set bandList to an empty list of a bim ifc band record
        set cornerCount to the length of cornerList
        set firstCorner to 0
        loop while (firstCorner + 2) < cornerCount:
            set first to the item at firstCorner in cornerList
            set second to the item at (firstCorner + 1) in cornerList
            set third to the item at (firstCorner + 2) in cornerList
            set firstCorner to firstCorner + 3
            if ((the absolute value of (second's z - first's z)) < 0.001) and ((the absolute value of (third's z - first's z)) < 0.001):
                set doubled to ((second's x - first's x) * (third's y - first's y)) - ((third's x - first's x) * (second's y - first's y))
                set wanted to doubled > 0.0
                if facesDown:
                    set wanted to doubled < 0.0
                if wanted and ((first's z > lowLimit) and (first's z < highLimit)):
                    set reachOne to (the cad dot of first and axis) - origin
                    set reachTwo to (the cad dot of second and axis) - origin
                    set reachThree to (the cad dot of third and axis) - origin
                    set reachLow to the minimum of reachOne and (the minimum of reachTwo and reachThree)
                    set reachHigh to the maximum of reachOne and (the maximum of reachTwo and reachThree)
                    set pieceArea to (the absolute value of doubled) * 0.5
                    set matched to -1
                    loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of bandList:
                        if matched < 0:
                            set levelBand to the item at bandCursor in bandList
                            if ((the absolute value of (levelBand's height - first's z)) < 0.002) and ((reachLow <= (levelBand's high + 0.002)) and (reachHigh >= (levelBand's low - 0.002))):
                                set matched to bandCursor
                    if matched >= 0:
                        set levelBand to the item at matched in bandList
                        replace item at index matched in bandList with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc band record, levelBand's height, the minimum of levelBand's low and reachLow, the maximum of levelBand's high and reachHigh, levelBand's area + pieceArea))
                    else:
                        append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc band record, first's z, reachLow, reachHigh, pieceArea)) to bandList
        return bandList

# The stretches from 0 to `fullLength` that the bands of `bandList` leave
# uncovered, each at least 0.1 long, as holes whose height is not yet known.
function the bim ifc gaps between {a pointer to a list:bandList} up to {a 64 bit floating-point number:fullLength}:
    execute:
        set gapList to an empty list of a bim ifc wall hole record
        set covered to 0.0
        set growing to true
        loop while growing:
            # As far as the bands that start within what is covered reach.
            set stretching to true
            loop while stretching:
                set stretching to false
                loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of bandList:
                    set levelBand to the item at bandCursor in bandList
                    if (levelBand's low <= (covered + 0.002)) and (levelBand's high > (covered + 0.000001)):
                        set covered to levelBand's high
                        set stretching to true
            # The next band after that, if any.
            set nextLow to fullLength
            loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of bandList:
                set levelBand to the item at bandCursor in bandList
                if (levelBand's low > (covered + 0.002)) and (levelBand's low < nextLow):
                    set nextLow to levelBand's low
            if (nextLow - covered) >= 0.1:
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc wall hole record, covered, nextLow, 0.0, 0.0)) to gapList
            if nextLow >= (fullLength - 0.002):
                set growing to false
            else:
                set covered to nextLow
        return gapList

function the bim ifc wall measured in {a pointer to a list:cornerList}:
    execute:
        set nowhere to a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0
        set wallResult to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc measured wall record, false, nowhere, nowhere, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, a cad topology list of a bim ifc wall hole record, false, 0.0)
        if (the length of cornerList) < 12:
            return wallResult
        set wallRun to the bim ifc main run of cornerList seen in plan true
        if (the cad length of wallRun) < 0.5:
            return wallResult
        # Of the two ways along its line, the one toward greater x (or y).
        if (wallRun's x < -0.000000001) or (((the absolute value of wallRun's x) <= 0.000000001) and (wallRun's y < 0.0)):
            set wallRun to wallRun scaled by -1.0
        set acrossAxis to a cad vector3 with x (0.0 - wallRun's y), y wallRun's x and z 0.0
        set alongSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along wallRun
        set acrossSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along acrossAxis
        set heightSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0)
        set wallLength to alongSpan's high - alongSpan's low
        set wallThickness to acrossSpan's high - acrossSpan's low
        set wallHeight to heightSpan's high - heightSpan's low
        if ((wallThickness < 0.03) or (wallThickness > 1.5)) or ((wallLength < 0.1) or (wallHeight < 0.1)):
            return wallResult
        set footArea to the bim ifc level area of cornerList at heightSpan's low
        set topArea to the bim ifc level area of cornerList at heightSpan's high
        set solidVolume to the bim ifc volume of cornerList
        set upright to ((the absolute value of (topArea - footArea)) <= (0.02 * footArea)) and ((the absolute value of (solidVolume - (footArea * wallHeight))) <= (0.02 * solidVolume))
        set middle to (acrossSpan's low + acrossSpan's high) * 0.5
        set wallResult's boxed to true
        set wallResult's volume to solidVolume
        set wallResult's start to a cad vector2 with x ((wallRun's x * alongSpan's low) + (acrossAxis's x * middle)) and y ((wallRun's y * alongSpan's low) + (acrossAxis's y * middle))
        set wallResult's finish to a cad vector2 with x ((wallRun's x * alongSpan's high) + (acrossAxis's x * middle)) and y ((wallRun's y * alongSpan's high) + (acrossAxis's y * middle))
        set wallResult's foot to heightSpan's low
        set wallResult's head to heightSpan's high
        set wallResult's thickness to wallThickness
        if upright and (footArea >= ((0.75 * wallLength) * wallThickness)):
            set wallResult's found to true
            set wallResult's start to a cad vector2 with x ((wallRun's x * alongSpan's low) + (acrossAxis's x * middle)) and y ((wallRun's y * alongSpan's low) + (acrossAxis's y * middle))
            set wallResult's finish to a cad vector2 with x ((wallRun's x * alongSpan's high) + (acrossAxis's x * middle)) and y ((wallRun's y * alongSpan's high) + (acrossAxis's y * middle))
            set wallResult's foot to heightSpan's low
            set wallResult's head to heightSpan's high
            set wallResult's thickness to wallThickness
            return wallResult
        # Not one prism: its box with rectangular holes right through it?
        # Where its top does not cover its length it is cut from above (a
        # window up to its head), where its foot does not, from below (a
        # door); cut both ways over the same stretch it is open over its
        # whole height. A cut from above ends on a band of triangles facing
        # up (its sill), one from below under a band facing down (its
        # head), and a hole inside it has both. The wall is its box less
        # those holes when its volume says so.
        set headBands to the bim ifc level bands of cornerList along wallRun from alongSpan's low facing down true above (heightSpan's low + 0.01) below (heightSpan's high + 1.0)
        set sillBands to the bim ifc level bands of cornerList along wallRun from alongSpan's low facing down false above (heightSpan's low + 0.01) below (heightSpan's high - 0.01)
        set topBands to the bim ifc level bands of cornerList along wallRun from alongSpan's low facing down false above (heightSpan's high - 0.002) below (heightSpan's high + 1.0)
        set footBands to the bim ifc level bands of cornerList along wallRun from alongSpan's low facing down true above (heightSpan's low - 1.0) below (heightSpan's low + 0.002)
        set topGaps to the bim ifc gaps between topBands up to wallLength
        set footGaps to the bim ifc gaps between footBands up to wallLength
        free topBands
        free footBands
        set holesFit to true
        set headUsed to an empty list of a boolean
        loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of headBands:
            append false to headUsed
        set sillUsed to an empty list of a boolean
        loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of sillBands:
            append false to sillUsed
        set footUsed to an empty list of a boolean
        loop gapCursor from 0 to the length of footGaps:
            append false to footUsed
        # Cut from above: open to the foot too, or down to a sill.
        loop gapCursor from 0 to the length of topGaps:
            set topGap to the item at gapCursor in topGaps
            set cutSill to heightSpan's low
            set cutFound to false
            loop footCursor from 0 to the length of footGaps:
                set footGap to the item at footCursor in footGaps
                if ((the absolute value of (footGap's low - topGap's low)) < 0.003) and ((the absolute value of (footGap's high - topGap's high)) < 0.003):
                    replace item at index footCursor in footUsed with true
                    set cutFound to true
            if cutFound = false:
                loop sillCursor from 0 to the length of sillBands:
                    set sillBand to the item at sillCursor in sillBands
                    if ((the absolute value of (sillBand's low - topGap's low)) < 0.003) and ((the absolute value of (sillBand's high - topGap's high)) < 0.003):
                        if (cutFound = false) or (sillBand's height > cutSill):
                            set cutSill to sillBand's height
                        set cutFound to true
                        replace item at index sillCursor in sillUsed with true
            if cutFound:
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc wall hole record, topGap's low, topGap's high, cutSill, heightSpan's high)) to (wallResult's holes's values)
            else:
                set holesFit to false
        # Cut from below only: up to a head.
        loop footCursor from 0 to the length of footGaps:
            if (the item at footCursor in footUsed) = false:
                set footGap to the item at footCursor in footGaps
                set cutHead to heightSpan's high
                set cutFound to false
                loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of headBands:
                    set headBand to the item at bandCursor in headBands
                    if ((the absolute value of (headBand's low - footGap's low)) < 0.003) and ((the absolute value of (headBand's high - footGap's high)) < 0.003):
                        if (cutFound = false) or (headBand's height < cutHead):
                            set cutHead to headBand's height
                        set cutFound to true
                        replace item at index bandCursor in headUsed with true
                if cutFound:
                    append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc wall hole record, footGap's low, footGap's high, heightSpan's low, cutHead)) to (wallResult's holes's values)
                else:
                    set holesFit to false
        # Holes inside it: a head over a sill.
        loop bandCursor from 0 to the length of headBands:
            if (the item at bandCursor in headUsed) = false:
                set headBand to the item at bandCursor in headBands
                set holeWide to headBand's high - headBand's low
                set holeSill to heightSpan's low
                set sillFound to false
                loop sillCursor from 0 to the length of sillBands:
                    set sillBand to the item at sillCursor in sillBands
                    if ((the absolute value of (sillBand's low - headBand's low)) < 0.003) and (((the absolute value of (sillBand's high - headBand's high)) < 0.003) and (sillBand's height < headBand's height)):
                        set holeSill to the maximum of holeSill and sillBand's height
                        set sillFound to true
                        replace item at index sillCursor in sillUsed with true
                if (sillFound = false) or ((the absolute value of (headBand's area - (holeWide * wallThickness))) > (0.03 * (holeWide * wallThickness))):
                    set holesFit to false
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc wall hole record, headBand's low, headBand's high, holeSill, headBand's height)) to (wallResult's holes's values)
        # A sill under nothing is a step, not a hole.
        loop sillCursor from 0 to the length of sillBands:
            if (the item at sillCursor in sillUsed) = false:
                set holesFit to false
        set holesArea to 0.0
        loop holeCursor from 0 to the length of (wallResult's holes's values):
            set cutOut to the item at holeCursor in (wallResult's holes's values)
            set holesArea to holesArea + ((cutOut's high - cutOut's low) * (cutOut's head - cutOut's sill))
            if ((cutOut's high - cutOut's low) < 0.1) or ((cutOut's head - cutOut's sill) < 0.1):
                set holesFit to false
        if (the length of (wallResult's holes's values)) = 0:
            set holesFit to false
        free headBands
        free sillBands
        free topGaps
        free footGaps
        free headUsed
        free sillUsed
        free footUsed
        set boxedVolume to wallThickness * ((wallLength * wallHeight) - holesArea)
        if holesFit and ((the absolute value of (solidVolume - boxedVolume)) <= (0.02 * solidVolume)):
            set middle to (acrossSpan's low + acrossSpan's high) * 0.5
            set wallResult's found to true
            set wallResult's start to a cad vector2 with x ((wallRun's x * alongSpan's low) + (acrossAxis's x * middle)) and y ((wallRun's y * alongSpan's low) + (acrossAxis's y * middle))
            set wallResult's finish to a cad vector2 with x ((wallRun's x * alongSpan's high) + (acrossAxis's x * middle)) and y ((wallRun's y * alongSpan's high) + (acrossAxis's y * middle))
            set wallResult's foot to heightSpan's low
            set wallResult's head to heightSpan's high
            set wallResult's thickness to wallThickness
        return wallResult

# A door or window measured from its triangles, for the wall it stands in to
# be found: the middle of its box on the plan, the direction it runs in,
# half its length along that and half its depth across it, its foot and
# head, and whether a wall has taken it as its opening's filling. `halfLong`
# 0 when it has no box to speak of.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc filling record
    members:
        source as an integer
        isDoor as a boolean
        centre as a cad vector2
        direction as a cad vector2
        halfLong as a 64 bit floating-point number
        halfDeep as a 64 bit floating-point number
        foot as a 64 bit floating-point number
        head as a 64 bit floating-point number
        taken as a boolean

function the bim ifc filling of {integer:sourceId} door {boolean:fillsDoor} boxed from {a pointer to a list:cornerList}:
    execute:
        set nowhere to a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0
        set fillingBox to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc filling record, sourceId, fillsDoor, nowhere, nowhere, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, false)
        if (the length of cornerList) < 12:
            return fillingBox
        set fillingRun to the bim ifc main run of cornerList seen in plan true
        if (the cad length of fillingRun) < 0.5:
            return fillingBox
        set acrossAxis to a cad vector3 with x (0.0 - fillingRun's y), y fillingRun's x and z 0.0
        set alongSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along fillingRun
        set acrossSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along acrossAxis
        set heightSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0)
        set middleAlong to (alongSpan's low + alongSpan's high) * 0.5
        set middleAcross to (acrossSpan's low + acrossSpan's high) * 0.5
        set fillingBox's centre to a cad vector2 with x ((fillingRun's x * middleAlong) + (acrossAxis's x * middleAcross)) and y ((fillingRun's y * middleAlong) + (acrossAxis's y * middleAcross))
        set fillingBox's direction to a cad vector2 with x fillingRun's x and y fillingRun's y
        set fillingBox's halfLong to (alongSpan's high - alongSpan's low) * 0.5
        set fillingBox's halfDeep to (acrossSpan's high - acrossSpan's low) * 0.5
        set fillingBox's foot to heightSpan's low
        set fillingBox's head to heightSpan's high
        return fillingBox

# The thickness of a native wall: the sum of its layers.
function the bim ifc layer sum of {bim ifc native wall record:nativeWall}:
    execute:
        set layerSum to 0.0
        loop layerCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeWall's layers's values):
            set layerSum to layerSum + (the item at layerCursor in (nativeWall's layers's values))'s thickness
        return layerSum

# Whether two native walls have the same layers.
function bim ifc pieces {bim ifc native wall record:firstWall} and {bim ifc native wall record:secondWall} are layered alike:
    execute:
        if (the length of (firstWall's layers's values)) != (the length of (secondWall's layers's values)):
            return false
        loop layerCursor from 0 to the length of (firstWall's layers's values):
            set firstLayer to the item at layerCursor in (firstWall's layers's values)
            set secondLayer to the item at layerCursor in (secondWall's layers's values)
            if (firstLayer's material != secondLayer's material) or ((the absolute value of (firstLayer's thickness - secondLayer's thickness)) > 0.0005):
                return false
        return true

# From where to where native wall `nativeWall` reaches along `axis` from
# `origin`, and how far its line lies across that (to the axis's left).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc wall stretch record
    members:
        low as a 64 bit floating-point number
        high as a 64 bit floating-point number
        across as a 64 bit floating-point number
        forward as a boolean

function the bim ifc stretch of {bim ifc native wall record:nativeWall} along {cad vector2:axis} from {cad vector2:origin}:
    execute:
        set startAlong to ((nativeWall's start's x - origin's x) * axis's x) + ((nativeWall's start's y - origin's y) * axis's y)
        set finishAlong to ((nativeWall's finish's x - origin's x) * axis's x) + ((nativeWall's finish's y - origin's y) * axis's y)
        set acrossValue to ((nativeWall's start's y - origin's y) * axis's x) - ((nativeWall's start's x - origin's x) * axis's y)
        return @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc wall stretch record, the minimum of startAlong and finishAlong, the maximum of startAlong and finishAlong, acrossValue, startAlong <= finishAlong)

# `openingList` with every two openings that stand right over one another
# (the same place and width along the wall) and touch or overlap made one
# opening over both heights: a strip of glazing through several storeys is
# given storey by storey, but the wall has one hole there. The lower one
# says whether it is a door.
function the bim ifc openings {cad topology list:openingList} with the stacked ones made one:
    execute:
        set merged to a cad topology list of a bim ifc native opening record
        loop openingCursor from 0 to the length of (openingList's values):
            set arriving to the item at openingCursor in (openingList's values)
            set absorbing to true
            loop while absorbing:
                set absorbing to false
                set takenAt to -1
                loop mergedCursor from 0 to the length of (merged's values):
                    if takenAt < 0:
                        set standing to the item at mergedCursor in (merged's values)
                        set samePlace to ((the absolute value of (standing's along - arriving's along)) < 0.005) and ((the absolute value of (standing's width - arriving's width)) < 0.005)
                        set touching to (arriving's sillHeight <= ((standing's sillHeight + standing's height) + 0.002)) and ((arriving's sillHeight + arriving's height) >= (standing's sillHeight - 0.002))
                        if samePlace and touching:
                            set takenAt to mergedCursor
                if takenAt >= 0:
                    set standing to the item at takenAt in (merged's values)
                    set lowest to the minimum of standing's sillHeight and arriving's sillHeight
                    set highest to the maximum of (standing's sillHeight + standing's height) and (arriving's sillHeight + arriving's height)
                    set lowerIsDoor to arriving's isDoor
                    if standing's sillHeight < arriving's sillHeight:
                        set lowerIsDoor to standing's isDoor
                    set arriving to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, standing's along, standing's width, highest - lowest, lowest, lowerIsDoor)
                    remove item takenAt from (merged's values)
                    set absorbing to true
            append arriving to (merged's values)
        return merged

# The doors and windows of `fillings` that stand between two pieces of wall
# on one line given the wall they lack: the two pieces (and one under and
# one over the gap, when the file has them) made one wall of `nativeSet`
# with the gap as its opening (see the top of this file). The pieces must
# be of one thickness, one line, one foot and head and the same layers, the
# gap free of other walls, and the door or window must fill it. How many
# were given a wall.
function join bim ifc wall pieces round {a pointer to a list:fillings} in {a pointer to a bim ifc native set record:nativeSet}:
    execute:
        set joined to 0
        loop fillingCursor from 0 to the length of fillings:
            set standing to the item at fillingCursor in fillings
            if (standing's taken = false) and ((standing's halfLong >= 0.15) and ((standing's head - standing's foot) >= 0.3)):
                set middleHeight to (standing's foot + standing's head) * 0.5
                set beforeIndex to -1
                set afterIndex to -1
                loop wallCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's walls's values):
                    if (the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)) < 0:
                        set candidate to the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's walls's values)
                        set lineX to candidate's finish's x - candidate's start's x
                        set lineY to candidate's finish's y - candidate's start's y
                        set lineLong to the square root of ((lineX * lineX) + (lineY * lineY))
                        if lineLong > 0.001:
                            if (the absolute value of (((lineX * standing's direction's y) - (lineY * standing's direction's x)) / lineLong)) < 0.02:
                                set pieceStretch to the bim ifc stretch of candidate along standing's direction from standing's centre
                                set touching to (the absolute value of pieceStretch's across) <= (((the bim ifc layer sum of candidate) * 0.5) + (standing's halfDeep + 0.02))
                                if touching and ((candidate's foot < middleHeight) and (candidate's head > middleHeight)):
                                    if (the absolute value of (pieceStretch's high + standing's halfLong)) < 0.08:
                                        set beforeIndex to wallCursor
                                    if (the absolute value of (pieceStretch's low - standing's halfLong)) < 0.08:
                                        set afterIndex to wallCursor
                if ((beforeIndex >= 0) and (afterIndex >= 0)) and (beforeIndex != afterIndex):
                    set beforeWall to the item at beforeIndex in (nativeSet's walls's values)
                    set afterWall to the item at afterIndex in (nativeSet's walls's values)
                    set beforeStretch to the bim ifc stretch of beforeWall along standing's direction from standing's centre
                    set afterStretch to the bim ifc stretch of afterWall along standing's direction from standing's centre
                    set wallThick to the bim ifc layer sum of beforeWall
                    set alike to ((the absolute value of (wallThick - (the bim ifc layer sum of afterWall))) < 0.002) and ((the absolute value of (beforeStretch's across - afterStretch's across)) < 0.002)
                    set alike to alike and (((the absolute value of (beforeWall's foot - afterWall's foot)) < 0.003) and ((the absolute value of (beforeWall's head - afterWall's head)) < 0.003))
                    set alike to alike and (bim ifc pieces beforeWall and afterWall are layered alike)
                    set gapLow to beforeStretch's high
                    set gapHigh to afterStretch's low
                    # The pieces under and over the gap, and anything else in it.
                    set underIndex to -1
                    set overIndex to -1
                    set blocked to false
                    loop wallCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's walls's values):
                        if ((the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)) < 0) and ((wallCursor != beforeIndex) and (wallCursor != afterIndex)):
                            set candidate to the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's walls's values)
                            set lineX to candidate's finish's x - candidate's start's x
                            set lineY to candidate's finish's y - candidate's start's y
                            set lineLong to the square root of ((lineX * lineX) + (lineY * lineY))
                            if lineLong > 0.001:
                                if (the absolute value of (((lineX * standing's direction's y) - (lineY * standing's direction's x)) / lineLong)) < 0.02:
                                    set pieceStretch to the bim ifc stretch of candidate along standing's direction from standing's centre
                                    set inLine to (the absolute value of (pieceStretch's across - beforeStretch's across)) < (wallThick * 0.5)
                                    set inGap to (pieceStretch's low < (gapHigh - 0.003)) and (pieceStretch's high > (gapLow + 0.003))
                                    set inHeight to (candidate's foot < (beforeWall's head - 0.003)) and (candidate's head > (beforeWall's foot + 0.003))
                                    if inLine and (inGap and inHeight):
                                        set fitsGap to ((the absolute value of (pieceStretch's low - gapLow)) < 0.003) and ((the absolute value of (pieceStretch's high - gapHigh)) < 0.003)
                                        set fitsGap to fitsGap and (((the absolute value of (pieceStretch's across - beforeStretch's across)) < 0.002) and ((the absolute value of ((the bim ifc layer sum of candidate) - wallThick)) < 0.002))
                                        set fitsGap to fitsGap and (bim ifc pieces beforeWall and candidate are layered alike)
                                        if fitsGap and (((the absolute value of (candidate's foot - beforeWall's foot)) < 0.003) and (underIndex < 0)):
                                            set underIndex to wallCursor
                                        else if fitsGap and (((the absolute value of (candidate's head - beforeWall's head)) < 0.003) and (overIndex < 0)):
                                            set overIndex to wallCursor
                                        else:
                                            set blocked to true
                    set gapSill to beforeWall's foot
                    if underIndex >= 0:
                        set gapSill to (the item at underIndex in (nativeSet's walls's values))'s head
                    set gapHead to beforeWall's head
                    if overIndex >= 0:
                        set gapHead to (the item at overIndex in (nativeSet's walls's values))'s foot
                    set gapWide to gapHigh - gapLow
                    set gapTall to gapHead - gapSill
                    # The door or window fills the gap.
                    set filledWide to (the minimum of standing's halfLong and gapHigh) - (the maximum of (0.0 - standing's halfLong) and gapLow)
                    set filledTall to (the minimum of standing's head and gapHead) - (the maximum of standing's foot and gapSill)
                    set fills to ((gapWide >= 0.3) and (gapTall >= 0.3)) and ((filledWide >= (0.8 * gapWide)) and (filledTall >= (0.8 * gapTall)))
                    if (alike and fills) and (blocked = false):
                        set beforeLong to beforeStretch's high - beforeStretch's low
                        set afterLong to afterStretch's high - afterStretch's low
                        set fromPoint to beforeWall's start
                        if beforeStretch's forward = false:
                            set fromPoint to beforeWall's finish
                        set toPoint to afterWall's finish
                        if afterStretch's forward = false:
                            set toPoint to afterWall's start
                        set openingList to a cad topology list of a bim ifc native opening record
                        loop openingCursor from 0 to the length of (beforeWall's openings's values):
                            set carried to the item at openingCursor in (beforeWall's openings's values)
                            set carriedAt to carried's along
                            if beforeStretch's forward = false:
                                set carriedAt to beforeLong - carried's along
                            append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, carriedAt, carried's width, carried's height, carried's sillHeight, carried's isDoor)) to (openingList's values)
                        append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, beforeLong + (gapWide * 0.5), gapWide, gapTall, gapSill, standing's isDoor)) to (openingList's values)
                        loop openingCursor from 0 to the length of (afterWall's openings's values):
                            set carried to the item at openingCursor in (afterWall's openings's values)
                            set carriedAt to carried's along
                            if afterStretch's forward = false:
                                set carriedAt to afterLong - carried's along
                            append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, (beforeLong + gapWide) + carriedAt, carried's width, carried's height, carried's sillHeight, carried's isDoor)) to (openingList's values)
                        replace item at index beforeIndex in (nativeSet's walls's values) with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native wall record, beforeWall's storey, fromPoint, toPoint, beforeWall's foot, beforeWall's head, beforeWall's layers, openingList))
                        replace item at index afterIndex in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values) with beforeIndex
                        if underIndex >= 0:
                            replace item at index underIndex in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values) with beforeIndex
                        if overIndex >= 0:
                            replace item at index overIndex in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values) with beforeIndex
                        replace item at index fillingCursor in fillings with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc filling record, standing's source, standing's isDoor, standing's centre, standing's direction, standing's halfLong, standing's halfDeep, standing's foot, standing's head, true))
                        append standing's source to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                        set joined to joined + 1
        return joined

# A member measured from its triangles, along the direction most of its
# edges run in (an upright one first tried along the height): `kind` 1 when
# every corner lies on a corner of its section's box (a rectangle, whatever
# cuts its ends), 2 when every corner lies on its circle, 3 for another
# section, 0 when it has none. Its axis from `start` to `finish` through the
# middle of its section's box, the box's `width` and `depth`, the `turn` of
# an upright one's width from the x axis, its section's area, and whether
# its corners lie further out along its width than along its depth (an I
# shape's web then lies along its width). For another section also what
# tells its kind: whether no corner lies outside the circle in its box (a
# tube), and whether corners lie near a middle line of its box (a web: an I
# shape has them, a hollow section does not).
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc measured member record
    members:
        kind as an integer
        start as a cad vector3
        finish as a cad vector3
        width as a 64 bit floating-point number
        depth as a 64 bit floating-point number
        turn as a 64 bit floating-point number
        sectionArea as a 64 bit floating-point number
        webAcross as a boolean
        roundOutline as a boolean
        webbed as a boolean

function the bim ifc member measured in {a pointer to a list:cornerList} standing {boolean:isStanding}:
    execute:
        set nowhere to a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
        set memberResult to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc measured member record, 0, nowhere, nowhere, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, false, false, false)
        set cornerCount to the length of cornerList
        if (cornerCount < 12) or (cornerCount > 30000):
            return memberResult
        set upward to a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0
        set solidVolume to the bim ifc volume of cornerList
        loop attempt from 0 to 2:
            set trying to (memberResult's kind = 0) or (memberResult's kind = 3)
            set memberAxis to upward
            if attempt = 1:
                set memberAxis to the bim ifc main run of cornerList seen in plan false
            if (attempt = 0) and (isStanding = false):
                set trying to false
            if (the cad length of memberAxis) < 0.5:
                set trying to false
            if trying:
                if memberAxis's z < 0.0:
                    set memberAxis to memberAxis scaled by -1.0
                set isUpright to (the absolute value of memberAxis's z) >= 0.99
                set widthAxis to the cad cross of memberAxis and upward
                if isUpright:
                    set widthAxis to the bim ifc main run of cornerList seen in plan true
                    if (the cad length of widthAxis) < 0.5:
                        set widthAxis to a cad vector3 with x 1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
                # Square to the axis.
                set widthAxis to the cad difference of widthAxis and (memberAxis scaled by (the cad dot of widthAxis and memberAxis))
                set widthSize to the cad length of widthAxis
                if widthSize > 0.000001:
                    set widthAxis to widthAxis scaled by (1.0 / widthSize)
                    set depthAxis to the cad cross of memberAxis and widthAxis
                    set widthSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along widthAxis
                    set depthSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along depthAxis
                    set lengthSpan to the bim ifc span of cornerList along memberAxis
                    set boxWidth to widthSpan's high - widthSpan's low
                    set boxDepth to depthSpan's high - depthSpan's low
                    set memberLength to lengthSpan's high - lengthSpan's low
                    if ((boxWidth > 0.001) and (boxDepth > 0.001)) and (memberLength > 0.01):
                        set middleAcross to (widthSpan's low + widthSpan's high) * 0.5
                        set middleDeep to (depthSpan's low + depthSpan's high) * 0.5
                        set cornered to true
                        set ringed to true
                        set spreadAcross to 0.0
                        set spreadDeep to 0.0
                        set farthest to 0.0
                        set nearMiddle to 0
                        loop cursor from 0 to cornerCount:
                            set spot to the item at cursor in cornerList
                            set acrossValue to the cad dot of spot and widthAxis
                            set deepValue to the cad dot of spot and depthAxis
                            set onSide to ((the absolute value of (acrossValue - widthSpan's low)) < 0.0005) or ((the absolute value of (acrossValue - widthSpan's high)) < 0.0005)
                            set onFace to ((the absolute value of (deepValue - depthSpan's low)) < 0.0005) or ((the absolute value of (deepValue - depthSpan's high)) < 0.0005)
                            if (onSide and onFace) = false:
                                set cornered to false
                            set radial to the square root of (((acrossValue - middleAcross) * (acrossValue - middleAcross)) + ((deepValue - middleDeep) * (deepValue - middleDeep)))
                            if (the absolute value of (radial - (boxWidth * 0.5))) > (0.01 * boxWidth):
                                set ringed to false
                            set farthest to the maximum of farthest and radial
                            if ((the absolute value of (acrossValue - middleAcross)) < (0.15 * boxWidth)) or ((the absolute value of (deepValue - middleDeep)) < (0.15 * boxDepth)):
                                set nearMiddle to nearMiddle + 1
                            set spreadAcross to spreadAcross + (the absolute value of (acrossValue - middleAcross))
                            set spreadDeep to spreadDeep + (the absolute value of (deepValue - middleDeep))
                        set filled to solidVolume / ((boxWidth * boxDepth) * memberLength)
                        set foundKind to 0
                        if cornered and (filled >= 0.7):
                            set foundKind to 1
                        else if (ringed and ((the absolute value of (boxWidth - boxDepth)) < (0.01 * boxWidth))) and ((filled >= 0.7) and (filled <= 0.8)):
                            set foundKind to 2
                        else if attempt = 1:
                            set foundKind to 3
                        if foundKind > 0:
                            set memberResult's kind to foundKind
                            set memberResult's start to the cad sum of (the cad sum of (widthAxis scaled by middleAcross) and (depthAxis scaled by middleDeep)) and (memberAxis scaled by lengthSpan's low)
                            set memberResult's finish to the cad sum of memberResult's start and (memberAxis scaled by memberLength)
                            set memberResult's width to boxWidth
                            set memberResult's depth to boxDepth
                            set memberResult's turn to 0.0
                            if isUpright:
                                set memberResult's turn to @intrinsic("atan2", widthAxis's y, widthAxis's x)
                            set memberResult's sectionArea to solidVolume / memberLength
                            set memberResult's webAcross to (spreadAcross / boxWidth) > (spreadDeep / boxDepth)
                            set memberResult's roundOutline to (farthest <= (0.53 * boxWidth)) and ((the absolute value of (boxWidth - boxDepth)) < (0.02 * boxWidth))
                            set memberResult's webbed to nearMiddle > 0
        return memberResult

# The native walls and slabs of `stepFile` (see the top of this file).
function the bim ifc natives of {bim step file record:stepFile}:
    execute:
        set nativeSet to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native set record, a cad topology list of a string, a cad topology list of a 64 bit floating-point number, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native wall record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native slab record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native linear record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native grid record, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of a bim pset entry record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native linear record, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer)
        if stepFile's valid = false:
            return nativeSet
        set reader to a fresh bim ifc reading of stepFile
        set r to the address of reader
        gather bim ifc units for r
        set nativeSet's grids to the bim ifc native grids in r
        set instanceCount to the length of (stepFile's starts)
        # The storeys, and what each instance is in.
        set storeyAt to an empty list of an integer
        set containerOf to an empty list of an integer
        set materialOf to an empty list of an integer
        set firstOpening to an empty list of an integer
        set nextOpening to an empty list of an integer
        set fillerOf to an empty list of an integer
        loop instanceCursor from 0 to instanceCount:
            append -1 to storeyAt
            append -1 to containerOf
            append -1 to materialOf
            append -1 to firstOpening
            append -1 to nextOpening
            append -1 to fillerOf
        set storeyIds to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCBUILDINGSTOREY") in stepFile
        loop storeyCursor from 0 to the length of storeyIds:
            set storeyId to the item at storeyCursor in storeyIds
            set storeyValue to the bim step instance storeyId in stepFile
            set storeyFrame to the bim ifc object axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of storeyValue) in storeyValue) in r
            replace item at index storeyId in storeyAt with (the length of (nativeSet's storeyNames's values))
            append (the bim step string of (the bim step argument 2 of storeyValue) in storeyValue) to (nativeSet's storeyNames's values)
            append storeyFrame's origin's z to (nativeSet's storeyElevations's values)
            append storeyId to (nativeSet's storeySources's values)
            # Its long name and description, which the level has no field
            # for, kept as properties of a set of their own.
            set longName to the bim step string of (the bim step argument 7 of storeyValue) in storeyValue
            if (the length of longName) > 0:
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim pset entry record, storeyId as a 64 bit integer, the string form of "IFC attributes", the string form of "LongName", the string form of "IFCLABEL", longName)) to (nativeSet's psets's values)
            set storeyNote to the bim step string of (the bim step argument 3 of storeyValue) in storeyValue
            if (the length of storeyNote) > 0:
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim pset entry record, storeyId as a 64 bit integer, the string form of "IFC attributes", the string form of "Description", the string form of "IFCTEXT", storeyNote)) to (nativeSet's psets's values)
            free bim step instance storeyValue
        free storeyIds
        record bim ifc containers of type (the string form of "IFCRELCONTAINEDINSPATIALSTRUCTURE") holding 4 in 5 in stepFile into containerOf
        record bim ifc containers of type (the string form of "IFCRELAGGREGATES") holding 5 in 4 in stepFile into containerOf
        # Materials, openings and their fillings.
        set relations to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCRELASSOCIATESMATERIAL") in stepFile
        loop relationCursor from 0 to the length of relations:
            set relation to the bim step instance (the item at relationCursor in relations) in stepFile
            set relatingMaterial to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of relation) in relation
            set related to the bim step argument 4 of relation
            loop memberCursor from 0 to the bim step count of related in relation:
                set member to the bim step reference of (the bim step member memberCursor of related in relation) in relation
                if (member >= 0) and (member < instanceCount):
                    replace item at index member in materialOf with relatingMaterial
            free bim step instance relation
        free relations
        set relations to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCRELVOIDSELEMENT") in stepFile
        loop relationCursor from 0 to the length of relations:
            set relation to the bim step instance (the item at relationCursor in relations) in stepFile
            set host to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 4 of relation) in relation
            set opening to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of relation) in relation
            if ((host >= 0) and (host < instanceCount)) and ((opening >= 0) and (opening < instanceCount)):
                replace item at index opening in nextOpening with (the item at host in firstOpening)
                replace item at index host in firstOpening with opening
            free bim step instance relation
        free relations
        set relations to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCRELFILLSELEMENT") in stepFile
        loop relationCursor from 0 to the length of relations:
            set relation to the bim step instance (the item at relationCursor in relations) in stepFile
            set opening to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 4 of relation) in relation
            if (opening >= 0) and (opening < instanceCount):
                replace item at index opening in fillerOf with (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of relation) in relation)
            free bim step instance relation
        free relations
        # The doors and windows, each boxed from its triangles, and where
        # each instance's box is kept (-1 none).
        set fillings to an empty list of a bim ifc filling record
        set fillingAt to an empty list of an integer
        loop instanceCursor from 0 to instanceCount:
            append -1 to fillingAt
        loop classCursor from 0 to 2:
            set fillingClass to the string form of "IFCDOOR"
            if classCursor = 1:
                set fillingClass to the string form of "IFCWINDOW"
            set fillingIds to the bim step instances of type fillingClass in stepFile
            loop cursor from 0 to the length of fillingIds:
                set fillingId to the item at cursor in fillingIds
                set fillingValue to the bim step instance fillingId in stepFile
                set fillingFrame to the bim ifc object axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of fillingValue) in fillingValue) in r
                set fillingBody to the bim ifc body of shape (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 6 of fillingValue) in fillingValue) in stepFile
                free bim step instance fillingValue
                set fillingCorners to the bim ifc corners of representation fillingBody through fillingFrame in r
                replace item at index fillingId in fillingAt with (the length of fillings)
                append (the bim ifc filling of fillingId door (classCursor = 0) boxed from fillingCorners) to fillings
                free fillingCorners
            free fillingIds
        # The walls.
        set wallIds to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCWALL") in stepFile
        set standardIds to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCWALLSTANDARDCASE") in stepFile
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of standardIds:
            append (the item at cursor in standardIds) to wallIds
        free standardIds
        loop wallCursor from 0 to the length of wallIds:
            set wallId to the item at wallCursor in wallIds
            set wallValue to the bim step instance wallId in stepFile
            set placementId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of wallValue) in wallValue
            set shapeId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 6 of wallValue) in wallValue
            free bim step instance wallValue
            set frame to the bim ifc object axes placementId in r
            set bodyId to the bim ifc body of shape shapeId in stepFile
            set extrusions to the bim ifc extrusions of representation bodyId through frame in r
            set made to false
            if extrusions's found:
                set vertical to true
                set foot to 1.0e30
                set head to -1.0e30
                loop sweepCursor from 0 to the length of (extrusions's sweeps's values):
                    set sweep to the item at sweepCursor in (extrusions's sweeps's values)
                    if (the absolute value of sweep's z) < (0.99 * (the cad length of sweep)):
                        set vertical to false
                set firstSweep to the item at 0 in (extrusions's sweeps's values)
                loop corner from 0 to the length of (extrusions's bottoms's values):
                    set bottom to the item at corner in (extrusions's bottoms's values)
                    set foot to the minimum of foot and (the minimum of bottom's z and (bottom's z + firstSweep's z))
                    set head to the maximum of head and (the maximum of bottom's z and (bottom's z + firstSweep's z))
                # The line's direction: the axis, else the footprint's
                # longest side.
                set axisPoints to the bim ifc axis of shape shapeId through frame in r
                set ux to 0.0
                set uy to 0.0
                if (the length of (axisPoints's values)) = 2:
                    set ux to (the item at 1 in (axisPoints's values))'s x - (the item at 0 in (axisPoints's values))'s x
                    set uy to (the item at 1 in (axisPoints's values))'s y - (the item at 0 in (axisPoints's values))'s y
                else:
                    set longest to 0.0
                    set ring to extrusions's firstRing's values
                    loop corner from 0 to the length of ring:
                        set here to the item at corner in ring
                        set following to the item at (the remainder of (corner + 1) divided by (the length of ring)) in ring
                        set sideLength to the square root of (((following's x - here's x) * (following's x - here's x)) + ((following's y - here's y) * (following's y - here's y)))
                        if sideLength > longest:
                            set longest to sideLength
                            set ux to following's x - here's x
                            set uy to following's y - here's y
                set axisLength to the square root of ((ux * ux) + (uy * uy))
                if vertical and (axisLength > 1e-6):
                    set ux to ux / axisLength
                    set uy to uy / axisLength
                    set nx to 0.0 - uy
                    set ny to ux
                    set alongLow to 1.0e30
                    set alongHigh to -1.0e30
                    set acrossLow to 1.0e30
                    set acrossHigh to -1.0e30
                    loop corner from 0 to the length of (extrusions's bottoms's values):
                        set bottom to the item at corner in (extrusions's bottoms's values)
                        set alongValue to (bottom's x * ux) + (bottom's y * uy)
                        set acrossValue to (bottom's x * nx) + (bottom's y * ny)
                        set alongLow to the minimum of alongLow and alongValue
                        set alongHigh to the maximum of alongHigh and alongValue
                        set acrossLow to the minimum of acrossLow and acrossValue
                        set acrossHigh to the maximum of acrossHigh and acrossValue
                    set thickness to acrossHigh - acrossLow
                    set middle to (acrossLow + acrossHigh) * 0.5
                    set startAlong to alongLow
                    set finishAlong to alongHigh
                    if (the length of (axisPoints's values)) = 2:
                        set startAlong to ((the item at 0 in (axisPoints's values))'s x * ux) + ((the item at 0 in (axisPoints's values))'s y * uy)
                        set finishAlong to ((the item at 1 in (axisPoints's values))'s x * ux) + ((the item at 1 in (axisPoints's values))'s y * uy)
                    # A straight wall's footprint is about its rectangle.
                    set ringArea to the absolute value of (the bim ifc plan area of (extrusions's firstRing's values))
                    set rectangleArea to (alongHigh - alongLow) * thickness
                    set squarish to (ringArea >= (0.75 * rectangleArea)) or ((the length of (extrusions's sweeps's values)) > 1)
                    if ((thickness >= 0.03) and (thickness <= 1.5)) and (((finishAlong - startAlong) >= 0.1) and squarish):
                        set startPoint to a cad vector2 with x ((ux * startAlong) + (nx * middle)) and y ((uy * startAlong) + (ny * middle))
                        set finishPoint to a cad vector2 with x ((ux * finishAlong) + (nx * middle)) and y ((uy * finishAlong) + (ny * middle))
                        set layerList to the bim ifc layers of material (the item at wallId in materialOf) thick thickness in r
                        set layerSum to 0.0
                        loop layerCursor from 0 to the length of (layerList's values):
                            set layerSum to layerSum + (the item at layerCursor in (layerList's values))'s thickness
                        if (the absolute value of (layerSum - thickness)) > 0.005:
                            set layerList to a cad topology list of a bim layer record
                            append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "concrete", thickness)) to (layerList's values)
                        set nativeWall to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native wall record, (the bim ifc storey of wallId among containerOf and storeyAt), startPoint, finishPoint, foot, head, layerList, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native opening record)
                        # Its openings, where their bodies cross it.
                        set openingAt to the item at wallId in firstOpening
                        loop while openingAt >= 0:
                            set openingValue to the bim step instance openingAt in stepFile
                            set openingFrame to the bim ifc object axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of openingValue) in openingValue) in r
                            set openingBody to the bim ifc body of shape (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 6 of openingValue) in openingValue) in stepFile
                            free bim step instance openingValue
                            set openingShape to the bim ifc extrusions of representation openingBody through openingFrame in r
                            if openingShape's found:
                                set openingLow to 1.0e30
                                set openingHigh to -1.0e30
                                set openingFoot to 1.0e30
                                set openingHead to -1.0e30
                                loop sweepCursor from 0 to the length of (openingShape's sweeps's values):
                                    set openingSweep to the item at sweepCursor in (openingShape's sweeps's values)
                                    loop corner from 0 to the length of (openingShape's bottoms's values):
                                        set bottom to the item at corner in (openingShape's bottoms's values)
                                        loop endCursor from 0 to 2:
                                            set spot to bottom
                                            if endCursor = 1:
                                                set spot to the cad sum of bottom and openingSweep
                                            set alongValue to ((spot's x * ux) + (spot's y * uy)) - startAlong
                                            set openingLow to the minimum of openingLow and alongValue
                                            set openingHigh to the maximum of openingHigh and alongValue
                                            set openingFoot to the minimum of openingFoot and spot's z
                                            set openingHead to the maximum of openingHead and spot's z
                                set filler to the item at openingAt in fillerOf
                                set fillingDoor to false
                                if filler >= 0:
                                    set fillingDoor to bim step instance filler is a "IFCDOOR" in stepFile
                                set openingWidth to openingHigh - openingLow
                                if ((openingWidth >= 0.1) and ((openingHead - openingFoot) >= 0.1)) and ((openingLow > -0.001) and (openingHigh < ((finishAlong - startAlong) + 0.001))):
                                    append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, ((openingLow + openingHigh) * 0.5), openingWidth, (openingHead - openingFoot), openingFoot, fillingDoor)) to (nativeWall's openings's values)
                                    if filler >= 0:
                                        append filler to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                                        if (the item at filler in fillingAt) >= 0:
                                            set takenBox to the item at (the item at filler in fillingAt) in fillings
                                            replace item at index (the item at filler in fillingAt) in fillings with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc filling record, takenBox's source, takenBox's isDoor, takenBox's centre, takenBox's direction, takenBox's halfLong, takenBox's halfDeep, takenBox's foot, takenBox's head, true))
                                    append openingAt to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                            set openingAt to the item at openingAt in nextOpening
                        append nativeWall to (nativeSet's walls's values)
                        append wallId to (nativeSet's wallSources's values)
                        append -1 to (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)
                        note bim ifc attributes of wallId in stepFile to (nativeSet's psets's values)
                        append wallId to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                        set made to true
            # Any other body, measured from its triangles.
            if made = false:
                set wallCorners to the bim ifc corners of representation bodyId through frame in r
                set measuredWall to the bim ifc wall measured in wallCorners
                free wallCorners
                # A mesh with its openings cut: the openings the file gives it.
                set givenOpenings to a cad topology list of a bim ifc native opening record
                set givenFillers to an empty list of an integer
                set givenIds to an empty list of an integer
                set byGiven to false
                if measuredWall's boxed and ((the item at wallId in firstOpening) >= 0):
                    set runX to measuredWall's finish's x - measuredWall's start's x
                    set runY to measuredWall's finish's y - measuredWall's start's y
                    set runLong to the square root of ((runX * runX) + (runY * runY))
                    set runX to runX / runLong
                    set runY to runY / runLong
                    set startAlong to (measuredWall's start's x * runX) + (measuredWall's start's y * runY)
                    set cutArea to 0.0
                    set openingAt to the item at wallId in firstOpening
                    loop while openingAt >= 0:
                        set openingValue to the bim step instance openingAt in stepFile
                        set openingFrame to the bim ifc object axes (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of openingValue) in openingValue) in r
                        set openingBody to the bim ifc body of shape (the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 6 of openingValue) in openingValue) in stepFile
                        free bim step instance openingValue
                        set openingCorners to the bim ifc corners of representation openingBody through openingFrame in r
                        if (the length of openingCorners) >= 12:
                            set openingLow to 1.0e30
                            set openingHigh to -1.0e30
                            set openingFoot to 1.0e30
                            set openingHead to -1.0e30
                            loop cornerCursor from 0 to the length of openingCorners:
                                set spot to the item at cornerCursor in openingCorners
                                set alongValue to ((spot's x * runX) + (spot's y * runY)) - startAlong
                                set openingLow to the minimum of openingLow and alongValue
                                set openingHigh to the maximum of openingHigh and alongValue
                                set openingFoot to the minimum of openingFoot and spot's z
                                set openingHead to the maximum of openingHead and spot's z
                            # What of it lies in the wall's box.
                            set openingLow to the maximum of openingLow and 0.0
                            set openingHigh to the minimum of openingHigh and runLong
                            set openingFoot to the maximum of openingFoot and measuredWall's foot
                            set openingHead to the minimum of openingHead and measuredWall's head
                            if ((openingHigh - openingLow) >= 0.1) and ((openingHead - openingFoot) >= 0.1):
                                set cutArea to cutArea + ((openingHigh - openingLow) * (openingHead - openingFoot))
                                set givenFiller to the item at openingAt in fillerOf
                                set givenDoor to false
                                if givenFiller >= 0:
                                    set givenDoor to bim step instance givenFiller is a "IFCDOOR" in stepFile
                                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, ((openingLow + openingHigh) * 0.5), openingHigh - openingLow, openingHead - openingFoot, openingFoot, givenDoor)) to (givenOpenings's values)
                                append givenFiller to givenFillers
                                append openingAt to givenIds
                        free openingCorners
                        set openingAt to the item at openingAt in nextOpening
                    # Its box less the openings, but for what a join cut from its
                    # ends; or its whole box, when the mesh leaves them uncut.
                    set boxedVolume to measuredWall's thickness * ((runLong * (measuredWall's head - measuredWall's foot)) - cutArea)
                    set wholeVolume to measuredWall's thickness * (runLong * (measuredWall's head - measuredWall's foot))
                    set cutFits to (measuredWall's volume >= (0.88 * boxedVolume)) and (measuredWall's volume <= (1.02 * boxedVolume))
                    set wholeFits to (measuredWall's volume >= (0.98 * wholeVolume)) and (measuredWall's volume <= (1.02 * wholeVolume))
                    if ((the length of givenIds) > 0) and (cutFits or wholeFits):
                        set byGiven to true
                if byGiven:
                    set layerList to the bim ifc layers of material (the item at wallId in materialOf) thick measuredWall's thickness in r
                    set layerSum to 0.0
                    loop layerCursor from 0 to the length of (layerList's values):
                        set layerSum to layerSum + (the item at layerCursor in (layerList's values))'s thickness
                    if (the absolute value of (layerSum - measuredWall's thickness)) > 0.005:
                        set layerList to a cad topology list of a bim layer record
                        append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "concrete", measuredWall's thickness)) to (layerList's values)
                    loop givenCursor from 0 to the length of givenIds:
                        append (the item at givenCursor in givenIds) to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                        set givenFiller to the item at givenCursor in givenFillers
                        if givenFiller >= 0:
                            append givenFiller to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                            if (the item at givenFiller in fillingAt) >= 0:
                                set takenBox to the item at (the item at givenFiller in fillingAt) in fillings
                                replace item at index (the item at givenFiller in fillingAt) in fillings with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc filling record, takenBox's source, takenBox's isDoor, takenBox's centre, takenBox's direction, takenBox's halfLong, takenBox's halfDeep, takenBox's foot, takenBox's head, true))
                    append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native wall record, (the bim ifc storey of wallId among containerOf and storeyAt), measuredWall's start, measuredWall's finish, measuredWall's foot, measuredWall's head, layerList, givenOpenings)) to (nativeSet's walls's values)
                    append wallId to (nativeSet's wallSources's values)
                    append -1 to (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)
                    note bim ifc attributes of wallId in stepFile to (nativeSet's psets's values)
                    append wallId to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                free givenFillers
                free givenIds
                if measuredWall's found and (byGiven = false):
                    set layerList to the bim ifc layers of material (the item at wallId in materialOf) thick measuredWall's thickness in r
                    set layerSum to 0.0
                    loop layerCursor from 0 to the length of (layerList's values):
                        set layerSum to layerSum + (the item at layerCursor in (layerList's values))'s thickness
                    if (the absolute value of (layerSum - measuredWall's thickness)) > 0.005:
                        set layerList to a cad topology list of a bim layer record
                        append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "concrete", measuredWall's thickness)) to (layerList's values)
                    # Each hole takes the door or window that fills most of it;
                    # a hole nothing fills leaves the wall imported.
                    set holeOpenings to a cad topology list of a bim ifc native opening record
                    set holeFillings to an empty list of an integer
                    set runX to measuredWall's finish's x - measuredWall's start's x
                    set runY to measuredWall's finish's y - measuredWall's start's y
                    set runLong to the square root of ((runX * runX) + (runY * runY))
                    set runX to runX / runLong
                    set runY to runY / runLong
                    set holesFilled to true
                    loop holeCursor from 0 to the length of (measuredWall's holes's values):
                        set wallHole to the item at holeCursor in (measuredWall's holes's values)
                        set bestFilling to -1
                        set bestCover to 0.6 * ((wallHole's high - wallHole's low) * (wallHole's head - wallHole's sill))
                        loop fillingCursor from 0 to the length of fillings:
                            set standing to the item at fillingCursor in fillings
                            set already to false
                            loop usedCursor from 0 to the length of holeFillings:
                                if (the item at usedCursor in holeFillings) = fillingCursor:
                                    set already to true
                            if ((standing's taken = false) and (already = false)) and ((standing's halfLong > 0.0) and ((the absolute value of ((runX * standing's direction's y) - (runY * standing's direction's x))) < 0.02)):
                                set offX to standing's centre's x - measuredWall's start's x
                                set offY to standing's centre's y - measuredWall's start's y
                                set alongCentre to (offX * runX) + (offY * runY)
                                set acrossCentre to (offY * runX) - (offX * runY)
                                if (the absolute value of acrossCentre) <= ((measuredWall's thickness * 0.5) + (standing's halfDeep + 0.02)):
                                    set coverWide to (the minimum of (alongCentre + standing's halfLong) and wallHole's high) - (the maximum of (alongCentre - standing's halfLong) and wallHole's low)
                                    set coverTall to (the minimum of standing's head and wallHole's head) - (the maximum of standing's foot and wallHole's sill)
                                    if ((coverWide > 0.0) and (coverTall > 0.0)) and ((coverWide * coverTall) > bestCover):
                                        set bestCover to coverWide * coverTall
                                        set bestFilling to fillingCursor
                        if bestFilling < 0:
                            set holesFilled to false
                        else:
                            append bestFilling to holeFillings
                            append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native opening record, (wallHole's low + wallHole's high) * 0.5, wallHole's high - wallHole's low, wallHole's head - wallHole's sill, wallHole's sill, (the item at bestFilling in fillings)'s isDoor)) to (holeOpenings's values)
                    if holesFilled:
                        loop usedCursor from 0 to the length of holeFillings:
                            set takenBox to the item at (the item at usedCursor in holeFillings) in fillings
                            replace item at index (the item at usedCursor in holeFillings) in fillings with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc filling record, takenBox's source, takenBox's isDoor, takenBox's centre, takenBox's direction, takenBox's halfLong, takenBox's halfDeep, takenBox's foot, takenBox's head, true))
                            append takenBox's source to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                        append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native wall record, (the bim ifc storey of wallId among containerOf and storeyAt), measuredWall's start, measuredWall's finish, measuredWall's foot, measuredWall's head, layerList, holeOpenings)) to (nativeSet's walls's values)
                        append wallId to (nativeSet's wallSources's values)
                        append -1 to (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)
                        note bim ifc attributes of wallId in stepFile to (nativeSet's psets's values)
                        append wallId to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
                    free holeFillings
        free wallIds
        # The doors and windows left standing between pieces of wall.
        ignore join bim ifc wall pieces round fillings in (the address of nativeSet)
        # Openings right over one another that touch are one opening.
        loop wallCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's walls's values):
            set stackedWall to the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's walls's values)
            if (the length of (stackedWall's openings's values)) > 1:
                replace item at index wallCursor in (nativeSet's walls's values) with (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native wall record, stackedWall's storey, stackedWall's start, stackedWall's finish, stackedWall's foot, stackedWall's head, stackedWall's layers, the bim ifc openings (stackedWall's openings) with the stacked ones made one))
        free fillings
        free fillingAt
        # The slabs (a roof's too).
        set slabIds to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCSLAB") in stepFile
        set standardSlabs to the bim step instances of type (the string form of "IFCSLABSTANDARDCASE") in stepFile
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of standardSlabs:
            append (the item at cursor in standardSlabs) to slabIds
        free standardSlabs
        loop slabCursor from 0 to the length of slabIds:
            set slabId to the item at slabCursor in slabIds
            set slabValue to the bim step instance slabId in stepFile
            set placementId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of slabValue) in slabValue
            set shapeId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 6 of slabValue) in slabValue
            free bim step instance slabValue
            set frame to the bim ifc object axes placementId in r
            set bodyId to the bim ifc body of shape shapeId in stepFile
            set extrusions to the bim ifc extrusions of representation bodyId through frame in r
            if extrusions's found and ((the length of (extrusions's sweeps's values)) = 1):
                set sweep to the item at 0 in (extrusions's sweeps's values)
                set ring to extrusions's firstRing's values
                if ((the absolute value of sweep's z) >= (0.99 * (the cad length of sweep))) and ((the length of ring) >= 3):
                    set outline to a cad topology list of a cad vector2
                    set ringFoot to 1.0e30
                    set ringTop to -1.0e30
                    loop corner from 0 to the length of ring:
                        set bottom to the item at corner in ring
                        append (a cad vector2 with x bottom's x and y bottom's y) to (outline's values)
                        set ringFoot to the minimum of ringFoot and (the minimum of bottom's z and (bottom's z + sweep's z))
                        set ringTop to the maximum of ringTop and (the maximum of bottom's z and (bottom's z + sweep's z))
                    set slabLayers to the bim ifc layers of material (the item at slabId in materialOf) thick (ringTop - ringFoot) in r
                    set slabMaterial to the string form of "concrete"
                    if (the length of (slabLayers's values)) > 0:
                        set slabMaterial to (the item at 0 in (slabLayers's values))'s material
                    append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native slab record, (the bim ifc storey of slabId among containerOf and storeyAt), outline, ringTop, (ringTop - ringFoot), slabMaterial)) to (nativeSet's slabs's values)
                    append slabId to (nativeSet's slabSources's values)
                    note bim ifc attributes of slabId in stepFile to (nativeSet's psets's values)
                    append slabId to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
        free slabIds
        # Columns, beams and piles, members, and the segments of pipes, ducts
        # and cable carriers.
        set memberIds to an empty list of an integer
        set memberRoles to an empty list of an integer
        loop classCursor from 0 to 7:
            set className to the string form of "IFCCOLUMN"
            set roleCode to bim column role
            if classCursor = 1:
                set className to the string form of "IFCBEAM"
                set roleCode to bim beam role
            if classCursor = 2:
                set className to the string form of "IFCPILE"
                set roleCode to bim pile role
            if classCursor = 3:
                set className to the string form of "IFCMEMBER"
                set roleCode to bim mullion role
            if classCursor = 4:
                set className to the string form of "IFCPIPESEGMENT"
                set roleCode to bim pipe role
            if classCursor = 5:
                set className to the string form of "IFCDUCTSEGMENT"
                set roleCode to bim duct role
            if classCursor = 6:
                set className to the string form of "IFCCABLECARRIERSEGMENT"
                set roleCode to bim cable tray role
            set classIds to the bim step instances of type className in stepFile
            loop cursor from 0 to the length of classIds:
                append (the item at cursor in classIds) to memberIds
                append roleCode to memberRoles
            free classIds
        loop memberCursor from 0 to the length of memberIds:
            set memberId to the item at memberCursor in memberIds
            set memberValue to the bim step instance memberId in stepFile
            set placementId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 5 of memberValue) in memberValue
            set shapeId to the bim step reference of (the bim step argument 6 of memberValue) in memberValue
            free bim step instance memberValue
            set frame to the bim ifc object axes placementId in r
            set section to the bim ifc section of representation (the bim ifc body of shape shapeId in stepFile) through frame in r
            if section's found:
                set memberLayers to the bim ifc layers of material (the item at memberId in materialOf) thick section's width in r
                set memberMaterial to the string form of "concrete"
                if (the length of (memberLayers's values)) > 0:
                    set memberMaterial to (the item at 0 in (memberLayers's values))'s material
                # A standing member turns its profile about its axis.
                set memberTurn to 0.0
                if (the absolute value of section's sweep's z) >= (0.99 * (the cad length of section's sweep)):
                    set memberTurn to @intrinsic("atan2", section's xAxis's y, section's xAxis's x)
                append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native linear record, (the bim ifc storey of memberId among containerOf and storeyAt), section's centre, (the cad sum of section's centre and section's sweep), section's width, section's depth, section's round, memberMaterial, (the item at memberCursor in memberRoles), memberTurn, 0.0, false, false, 0 as a 64 bit integer)) to (nativeSet's linears's values)
                append memberId to (nativeSet's linearSources's values)
                note bim ifc attributes of memberId in stepFile to (nativeSet's psets's values)
                append memberId to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
            else:
                # Any other body, measured from its triangles.
                set memberCorners to the bim ifc corners of representation (the bim ifc body of shape shapeId in stepFile) through frame in r
                set measuredMember to the bim ifc member measured in memberCorners standing ((the item at memberCursor in memberRoles) = bim column role)
                free memberCorners
                # A segment is hollow: it counts by its outline. With no
                # material in the file it is taken to be steel.
                set memberRole to the item at memberCursor in memberRoles
                set isSegment to ((memberRole = bim pipe role) or (memberRole = bim duct role)) or (memberRole = bim cable tray role)
                if isSegment and (measuredMember's kind = 3):
                    set measuredMember's kind to 1
                    if measuredMember's roundOutline:
                        set measuredMember's kind to 2
                if measuredMember's kind > 0:
                    set memberLayers to the bim ifc layers of material (the item at memberId in materialOf) thick measuredMember's width in r
                    set memberMaterial to the string form of "concrete"
                    if (the length of (memberLayers's values)) > 0:
                        set memberMaterial to (the item at 0 in (memberLayers's values))'s material
                    if isSegment and ((the item at memberId in materialOf) < 0):
                        set memberMaterial to the string form of "steel"
                    set measuredLinear to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native linear record, (the bim ifc storey of memberId among containerOf and storeyAt), measuredMember's start, measuredMember's finish, measuredMember's width, measuredMember's depth, ((measuredMember's kind = 2) or measuredMember's roundOutline), memberMaterial, (the item at memberCursor in memberRoles), measuredMember's turn, measuredMember's sectionArea, measuredMember's webbed, measuredMember's webAcross, 0 as a 64 bit integer)
                    note bim ifc attributes of memberId in stepFile to (nativeSet's psets's values)
                    if measuredMember's kind = 3:
                        append measuredLinear to (nativeSet's shaped's values)
                        append memberId to (nativeSet's shapedSources's values)
                    else:
                        append measuredLinear to (nativeSet's linears's values)
                        append memberId to (nativeSet's linearSources's values)
                        append memberId to (nativeSet's skipped's values)
        free memberIds
        # The property sets of what was made native and of the storeys.
        set wanted to an empty list of a boolean
        loop instanceCursor from 0 to instanceCount:
            append false to wanted
        mark bim ifc sources (nativeSet's storeySources's values) in wanted
        mark bim ifc sources (nativeSet's wallSources's values) in wanted
        mark bim ifc sources (nativeSet's slabSources's values) in wanted
        mark bim ifc sources (nativeSet's linearSources's values) in wanted
        mark bim ifc sources (nativeSet's shapedSources's values) in wanted
        set gathered to the bim ifc psets of stepFile wanted wanted scaled reader's lengthScale
        loop psetCursor from 0 to the length of gathered:
            append (the item at psetCursor in gathered) to (nativeSet's psets's values)
        free gathered
        free wanted
        free memberRoles
        free storeyAt
        free containerOf
        free materialOf
        free firstOpening
        free nextOpening
        free fillerOf
        return nativeSet

# The signed area of a ring of points seen from above.
function the bim ifc plan area of {a pointer to a list:ring}:
    execute:
        set doubledArea to 0.0
        loop corner from 0 to the length of ring:
            set here to the item at corner in ring
            set following to the item at (the remainder of (corner + 1) divided by (the length of ring)) in ring
            set doubledArea to doubledArea + ((here's x * following's y) - (following's x * here's y))
        return doubledArea * 0.5

# What `add bim ifc natives` made.
class:
    patterns:
        [a|] bim ifc native count record
    members:
        levels as an integer
        walls as an integer
        openings as an integer
        slabs as an integer
        linears as an integer
        grids as an integer

# The instances in `sources` marked in `wanted`.
local function mark bim ifc sources {a pointer to a list:sourceList} in {a pointer to a list:wanted}:
    execute:
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of sourceList:
            set sourceId to the item at cursor in sourceList
            if (sourceId >= 0) and (sourceId < (the length of wanted)):
                replace item at index sourceId in wanted with true

# The storey (a level of `target`) for the natives' storey `storeyIndex`:
# an existing level at its elevation, or a new one; the first level when it
# has none.
function the bim level for ifc storey {integer:storeyIndex} of {bim ifc native set record:natives} in {a pointer to a bim model record:target} counting {a pointer to a bim ifc native count record:counts}:
    execute:
        if (storeyIndex < 0) or (storeyIndex >= (the length of (natives's storeyNames's values))):
            return (the item at 0 in (target's levels's values))'s id
        set elevation to the item at storeyIndex in (natives's storeyElevations's values)
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (target's levels's values):
            set levelValue to the item at cursor in (target's levels's values)
            if (the absolute value of (levelValue's elevation - elevation)) < 0.005:
                return levelValue's id
        set storeyHeight to 3.0
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (natives's storeyElevations's values):
            set other to the item at cursor in (natives's storeyElevations's values)
            if (other > (elevation + 0.5)) and ((other - elevation) < storeyHeight):
                set storeyHeight to other - elevation
        set counts's levels to counts's levels + 1
        return add bim level named (the item at storeyIndex in (natives's storeyNames's values)) at elevation with height storeyHeight to target

# The wall type of `target` with these layers, or a new one (named by the
# rules).
function the bim wall type with layers {a pointer to a list:layerList} in {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (target's wallTypes's values):
            set candidate to the item at cursor in (target's wallTypes's values)
            if (candidate's role = bim wall planar role) and ((the length of (candidate's layers's values)) = (the length of layerList)):
                set same to true
                loop layerCursor from 0 to the length of layerList:
                    set wanted to the item at layerCursor in layerList
                    set have to the item at layerCursor in (candidate's layers's values)
                    if (wanted's material != have's material) or ((the absolute value of (wanted's thickness - have's thickness)) > 0.0005):
                        set same to false
                if same:
                    return candidate's id
        return add bim wall type named (the string form of "IFC") with layerList to target

# The linear type of `target` for a native member: one of its role, size,
# shape and material, or a new one (named by the rules).
function the bim linear type for {bim ifc native linear record:nativeLinear} in {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (target's linearTypes's values):
            set candidate to the item at cursor in (target's linearTypes's values)
            if ((candidate's role = nativeLinear's role) and (candidate's round = nativeLinear's round)) and (candidate's material = nativeLinear's material):
                if ((the absolute value of (candidate's width - nativeLinear's width)) < 0.0005) and ((the absolute value of (candidate's depth - nativeLinear's depth)) < 0.0005):
                    return candidate's id
        return add bim linear type named (the string form of "IFC") as role nativeLinear's role sized nativeLinear's width by nativeLinear's depth round nativeLinear's round of nativeLinear's material to target

# The opening type of `target` of this rough size (a door type standing on
# the floor when `isDoor`) whose rough opening keeps `frameWidth` beside and
# above the opening itself, or a new one.
function the bim opening type sized {a 64 bit floating-point number:roughWidth} by {a 64 bit floating-point number:roughHeight} on {a 64 bit floating-point number:sillValue} framed {a 64 bit floating-point number:frameWidth} door {boolean:isDoor} in {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (target's openingTypes's values):
            set candidate to the item at cursor in (target's openingTypes's values)
            if ((candidate's isDoor = isDoor) and ((the absolute value of (candidate's frame - frameWidth)) < 0.0005)) and (((the absolute value of ((the bim rough width of candidate) - roughWidth)) < 0.002) and ((the absolute value of ((the bim rough height of candidate) - roughHeight)) < 0.002)):
                if isDoor or ((the absolute value of (candidate's sill - sillValue)) < 0.002):
                    return candidate's id
        if isDoor:
            return add bim door type named (the string form of "Deur") sized (roughWidth - (2.0 * frameWidth)) by (roughHeight - frameWidth) with frame frameWidth to target
        return add bim opening type named (the string form of "Raam") sized (roughWidth - (2.0 * frameWidth)) by (roughHeight - frameWidth) with sill sillValue and frame frameWidth to target

# The natives added to `target` (inside a transaction the caller opens):
# their storeys as levels, walls with their types and openings, slabs.
function add bim ifc natives {bim ifc native set record:nativeSet} to {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        set counts to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native count record, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
        if (the length of (target's levels's values)) = 0:
            ignore add bim level named (the string form of "Ground floor") at 0.0 with height 3.0 to target
        # Every storey a level, with the storey's properties (given again,
        # not doubled, when the same file is imported twice).
        loop storeyCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's storeySources's values):
            set storeyLevelId to the bim level for ifc storey storeyCursor of nativeSet in target counting (the address of counts)
            set bim ifc psets of (the item at storeyCursor in (nativeSet's storeySources's values)) in (nativeSet's psets's values) on storeyLevelId in target
        # What an earlier import of the same file made native is left out
        # (it is in the model already, maybe changed); what is made now is
        # listed as taken over, by its GlobalId.
        refresh bim shared grid heights in target
        set takenIds to the bim promoted ids of (@intrinsic("dereference", target))
        # The properties by the instance they belong to, and the GlobalIds
        # listed in this pass.
        set psetIndex to the bim pset index of (nativeSet's psets's values)
        set notedIds to an empty list of a string
        loop gridCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's grids's values):
            set nativeGrid to the item at gridCursor in (nativeSet's grids's values)
            if (bim guid nativeGrid's sourceKey is among takenIds) = false:
                set gridHigh to nativeGrid's elevation + 3.0
                loop levelCursor from 0 to the length of (target's levels's values):
                    set levelValue to the item at levelCursor in (target's levels's values)
                    set gridHigh to the maximum of gridHigh and (levelValue's elevation + levelValue's height)
                if nativeGrid's top > nativeGrid's elevation:
                    set gridHigh to nativeGrid's top
                set freshGrid to add bim grid named nativeGrid's name from nativeGrid's start to nativeGrid's finish reaching nativeGrid's elevation to gridHigh to target
                if freshGrid != the bim refused id:
                    set counts's grids to counts's grids + 1
                    note bim guid nativeGrid's sourceKey promoted as freshGrid in target
                    append nativeGrid's sourceKey to takenIds
        # The element each wall became (the refused id for none), for the
        # pieces made part of another wall to be listed as taken over into it.
        set wallElements to an empty list of a 64 bit integer
        loop wallCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's walls's values):
            set nativeWall to the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's walls's values)
            set wallSource to the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's wallSources's values)
            set wallGuid to the bim ifc global id of indexed source wallSource through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values)
            append (the bim refused id) to wallElements
            set standsAlone to true
            if wallCursor < (the length of (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)):
                set standsAlone to (the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)) < 0
            if standsAlone and ((bim guid wallGuid is among takenIds) = false):
                set levelId to the bim level for ifc storey nativeWall's storey of nativeSet in target counting (the address of counts)
                set levelElevation to (the item at (the bim level index of levelId in (@intrinsic("dereference", target)))'s position in (target's levels's values))'s elevation
                set typeId to the bim wall type with layers (nativeWall's layers's values) in target
                set fresh to add bim wall typed typeId on levelId from nativeWall's start to nativeWall's finish to target
                if fresh != the bim refused id:
                    replace item at index wallCursor in wallElements with fresh
                    set counts's walls to counts's walls + 1
                    hand bim ifc psets of source wallSource through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values) to fresh in target
                    note bim guid wallGuid first promoted as fresh besides notedIds in target
                    ignore set bim wall fresh base to (nativeWall's foot - levelElevation) and height to (nativeWall's head - nativeWall's foot) in target
                    loop openingCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeWall's openings's values):
                        set nativeOpening to the item at openingCursor in (nativeWall's openings's values)
                        # A door stands on its level: its head stays where the
                        # file has it, whatever lies under the level is not its.
                        set openingSill to nativeOpening's sillHeight - levelElevation
                        set openingWide to nativeOpening's width
                        set openingHigh to nativeOpening's height
                        set openingHead to openingSill + openingHigh
                        # What of it lies over the wall's top or under its foot is
                        # not the wall's: the model builds no wall whose opening
                        # leaves it.
                        set wallTop to nativeWall's head - levelElevation
                        set wallFoot to nativeWall's foot - levelElevation
                        if openingHead > wallTop:
                            set openingHead to wallTop
                        if (openingSill < wallFoot) and (nativeOpening's isDoor = false):
                            set openingSill to wallFoot
                        set openingHigh to openingHead - openingSill
                        if nativeOpening's isDoor:
                            set openingHigh to openingHead
                        # An opening as large as its wall leaves nothing of the
                        # wall, and the model refuses it. The opening then keeps
                        # its own size and gives up the margin round it: the
                        # wall's rim stands for the frame.
                        set openingFrame to 0.05
                        set hostAcross to nativeWall's finish's x - nativeWall's start's x
                        set hostAlong to nativeWall's finish's y - nativeWall's start's y
                        set hostLong to the square root of ((hostAcross * hostAcross) + (hostAlong * hostAlong))
                        set besideClear to the minimum of (nativeOpening's along - (openingWide * 0.5)) and ((hostLong - nativeOpening's along) - (openingWide * 0.5))
                        set reachesEnd to besideClear <= 0.000001
                        set reachesHead to openingHead >= ((nativeWall's head - levelElevation) - 0.000001)
                        if reachesEnd or reachesHead:
                            set openingFrame to 0.0
                            if reachesEnd:
                                set openingWide to openingWide - 0.1
                            if reachesHead:
                                set openingHigh to openingHigh - 0.05
                        set openingTypeId to the bim refused id
                        if (openingWide >= 0.1) and (openingHigh >= 0.1):
                            set openingTypeId to the bim opening type sized openingWide by openingHigh on openingSill framed openingFrame door nativeOpening's isDoor in target
                        if openingTypeId != the bim refused id:
                            if (add bim opening typed openingTypeId in fresh at nativeOpening's along to target) != the bim refused id:
                                set counts's openings to counts's openings + 1
        loop wallCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values):
            set intoWall to the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)
            if intoWall >= 0:
                # The wall it is part of may itself have been made part of another.
                set hops to 0
                loop while ((the item at intoWall in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)) >= 0) and (hops < 64):
                    set intoWall to the item at intoWall in (nativeSet's wallAbsorbed's values)
                    set hops to hops + 1
                set intoElement to the item at intoWall in wallElements
                if intoElement != the bim refused id:
                    set pieceGuid to the bim ifc global id of indexed source (the item at wallCursor in (nativeSet's wallSources's values)) through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values)
                    if (bim guid pieceGuid is among takenIds) = false:
                        note bim guid pieceGuid first promoted as intoElement besides notedIds in target
        free wallElements
        loop slabCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's slabs's values):
            set nativeSlab to the item at slabCursor in (nativeSet's slabs's values)
            set slabSource to the item at slabCursor in (nativeSet's slabSources's values)
            set slabGuid to the bim ifc global id of indexed source slabSource through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values)
            if (bim guid slabGuid is among takenIds) = false:
                set levelId to the bim level for ifc storey nativeSlab's storey of nativeSet in target counting (the address of counts)
                set levelElevation to (the item at (the bim level index of levelId in (@intrinsic("dereference", target)))'s position in (target's levels's values))'s elevation
                set fresh to add bim slab on levelId around (nativeSlab's outline's values) thick nativeSlab's thickness to target
                if fresh != the bim refused id:
                    set counts's slabs to counts's slabs + 1
                    hand bim ifc psets of source slabSource through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values) to fresh in target
                    note bim guid slabGuid first promoted as fresh besides notedIds in target
                    ignore set bim slab fresh material to nativeSlab's material in target
                    ignore set bim plate fresh top to (nativeSlab's top - levelElevation) pitch 0.0 heading 0.0 in target
        loop linearCursor from 0 to the length of (nativeSet's linears's values):
            set nativeLinear to the item at linearCursor in (nativeSet's linears's values)
            set linearSource to the item at linearCursor in (nativeSet's linearSources's values)
            set linearGuid to the bim ifc global id of indexed source linearSource through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values)
            if (bim guid linearGuid is among takenIds) = false:
                set levelId to the bim level for ifc storey nativeLinear's storey of nativeSet in target counting (the address of counts)
                set levelElevation to (the item at (the bim level index of levelId in (@intrinsic("dereference", target)))'s position in (target's levels's values))'s elevation
                set typeId to the bim linear type for nativeLinear in target
                set fromSpot to a cad vector3 with x nativeLinear's start's x, y nativeLinear's start's y and z (nativeLinear's start's z - levelElevation)
                set toSpot to a cad vector3 with x nativeLinear's finish's x, y nativeLinear's finish's y and z (nativeLinear's finish's z - levelElevation)
                set freshLinear to add bim linear typed typeId on levelId from fromSpot to toSpot turned nativeLinear's turn to target
                if freshLinear != the bim refused id:
                    set counts's linears to counts's linears + 1
                    hand bim ifc psets of source linearSource through psetIndex of (nativeSet's psets's values) to freshLinear in target
                    note bim guid linearGuid first promoted as freshLinear besides notedIds in target
        free takenIds
        free notedIds
        free bim pset index psetIndex
        return counts

# The IFC file at `path` imported: its walls and slabs made native elements
# of `documentValue`'s model (one undoable step, what was made counted in
# `counts`), the rest as imported read-only elements.
function the bim ifc import of {a string:path} made native in {a pointer to a bim document record:documentValue} counting {a pointer to a bim ifc native count record:counts}:
    execute:
        set stepFile to the bim step file at path
        set nativeSet to the bim ifc natives of stepFile
        set madeCounts to the bim ifc natives nativeSet made in documentValue
        set counts's levels to madeCounts's levels
        set counts's walls to madeCounts's walls
        set counts's openings to madeCounts's openings
        set counts's slabs to madeCounts's slabs
        set counts's linears to madeCounts's linears
        set counts's grids to madeCounts's grids
        return the bim ifc elements of stepFile skipping (nativeSet's skipped's values)

# Adds the walls, slabs, linear elements and straight grids of `nativeSet` to
# `documentValue`'s model as one undoable step (none when there are none);
# what was made, counted.
function the bim ifc natives {bim ifc native set record:nativeSet} made in {a pointer to a bim document record:documentValue}:
    execute:
        set madeCounts to @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native count record, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
        if (((the length of (nativeSet's walls's values)) + (the length of (nativeSet's slabs's values))) + ((the length of (nativeSet's linears's values)) + (the length of (nativeSet's grids's values)))) > 0:
            begin bim transaction in documentValue
            set madeCounts to add bim ifc natives nativeSet to (the address of (documentValue's current))
            commit bim transaction in documentValue
        return madeCounts

# No natives (nothing to make native).
function no bim ifc natives:
    execute:
        return @intrinsic("construct", a bim ifc native set record, a cad topology list of a string, a cad topology list of a 64 bit floating-point number, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native wall record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native slab record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native linear record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native grid record, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of a bim pset entry record, a cad topology list of a bim ifc native linear record, a cad topology list of an integer, a cad topology list of an integer)

# What was made native, for a message: "12 walls, 30 openings, 4 floors
# made native, 2 storeys added; ".
function the bim ifc native text of {bim ifc native count record:counts}:
    execute:
        if (((counts's walls + counts's slabs) + counts's linears) + counts's grids) = 0:
            return the string form of ""
        set described to (((the string form of counts's walls) + (the string form of " walls, ")) + ((the string form of counts's openings) + (the string form of " openings, "))) + ((the string form of counts's slabs) + (the string form of " floors, "))
        set described to (described + (the string form of counts's linears)) + (the string form of " columns and beams made native")
        if counts's grids > 0:
            set described to (described + (the string form of ", ")) + ((the string form of counts's grids) + (the string form of " grids"))
        if counts's levels > 0:
            set described to (described + (the string form of ", ")) + ((the string form of counts's levels) + (the string form of " storeys added"))
        return described + (the string form of "; ")
